    description: "Concentrating all study into one block does raise immediate test scores and can be rational when an exam is hours away and long-term memory is not the goal. But across the spacing literature (Cepeda et al., 2006; Latimier et al., 2021, g = 0.74 favoring spacing) massed study produces markedly worse retention days to weeks later than the identical time spread out. Its main documented downside is the fluency it creates during study, which learners misread as durable learning.",
