    description: "Deliberately ask 'what are the reasons my judgment might be wrong?' or 'how would this look if the opposite were true?' Lord, Lepper & Preston showed that a consider-the-opposite instruction reduced biased assimilation and hypothesis-confirmation more than simply telling people to be fair and unbiased. The same move (consider-an-alternative) reliably shrinks anchoring, overconfidence and hindsight bias.",
