    description: "Zone 2 (aerobic work below the first lactate threshold, blood lactate ~<2 mmol/L) is marketed as the 'optimal' intensity for mitochondrial and metabolic health. A 2025 Sports Medicine narrative review found current evidence does NOT support that claim: higher-intensity work drives at least as much mitochondrial biogenesis and larger VO₂max gains, and a 2024 RCT found brief vigorous 'exercise snacks' improved cardiorespiratory fitness at least as well as time-matched moderate continuous training. Low-intensity aerobic volume is genuinely useful (recoverable, safe for beginners, builds an aerobic base) — its claimed unique superiority is not.",
