    description: "Annual flu vaccination offers modest, real protection in healthy adults. The Cochrane review (Demicheli 2018; 80,000+ adults across 52 trials) found about 71 healthy adults must be vaccinated to prevent one lab-confirmed influenza case and about 29 to prevent one influenza-like illness. Effects on hospitalization and death in otherwise-healthy young adults are small and uncertain; the clearest benefit is in older and high-risk people.",
    callout: "Educational, not medical advice; discuss with a clinician. Efficacy swings year to year with strain match and is lower in the elderly; the strongest rationale is population and high-risk protection, not dramatic personal protection in healthy young adults. Cochrane also flagged incomplete reporting in ~70% of included trials.",
