    description: "A disproportionate pull to keep whatever is currently in place — the default plan, incumbent supplier, existing portfolio — even when a better alternative with identical risk-return exists. Samuelson & Zeckhauser (1988) showed in lab and field data (health-plan and pension enrollment) that people stick to a designated status quo at rates several times higher than they choose it fresh. Someone high in this bias under-switches, leaves better options on the table, and adapts too slowly to changed conditions.",
