    degrades: ["integration of interdependent work", "handoff reliability", "throughput and rework"],
    description: "Steiner showed actual group productivity = potential productivity minus process losses from faulty coordination and motivation. Heath & Staudenmayer identified 'coordination neglect': people's lay theories of organizing over-focus on dividing labor and systematically undervalue the integration work of reconnecting the pieces, so specialists optimize locally while handoffs, interfaces, and shared understanding decay. The result is duplicated effort, dropped handoffs, and rework that make a team deliver less than its members could individually.",
