    degrades: ["pooling of unique knowledge", "decision accuracy", "use of expert input"],
    description: "Group discussion is dominated by information members already hold in common, while unique facts held by only one person get raised less and are quickly dropped — so groups often miss the 'hidden profile' answer that only emerges when all information is pooled. Stasser & Titus first demonstrated this biased sampling; Lu, Yuan & McLeod's meta-analysis of 25 years of hidden-profile work confirmed groups are far less likely to solve hidden-profile than manifest-profile problems. Mesmer-Magnus & DeChurch's meta-analysis (72 studies, N ≈ 17,000) found unique information sharing strongly predicts team performance, yet teams share far too little of it.",
