    description: "Even when systems are designed to share knowledge, employees intentionally conceal what they know — Connelly et al. defined and validated 'knowledge hiding' (evasive hiding, playing dumb, rationalized hiding) as distinct from simply lacking knowledge. Hiding is driven by distrust and a competitive climate and, critically, tends to be reciprocated: hiding provokes hiding back, degrading the whole information ecosystem and hardening silos that block collective problem-solving.",
