    description: "The classic claim is that self-control draws on a limited resource that 'depletes,' so exerting willpower on one task leaves you weaker on the next (ego depletion / decision fatigue). Included here honestly because it is popular but weak: a 23-lab preregistered replication (N=2,141) found essentially no depletion effect (near-zero d), and subsequent bias-corrected meta-analyses put the true effect near zero. Self-control failures are real, but the specific 'muscle that runs out of fuel' explanation is not reliably supported.",
