    degrades: ["intrinsic motivation", "work engagement", "initiative", "retention"],
    description: "Controlling, low-autonomy-support leadership is the inverse of what motivates people. Slemp et al.'s meta-analysis (72 studies, 83 samples, N=32,870) found leader autonomy support correlates strongly with autonomous motivation, need satisfaction, well-being, and positive work behaviors, and negatively with distress; withholding it removes the largest lever on engagement. Kim, Beehr & Prewett's meta-analysis (55 samples) showed empowering leadership relates to attitudes toward the leader at rho=.59 and to performance at rho=.31 — so over-control most directly poisons the relationship and motivation.",
