    description: "Trust in close relationships is built on demonstrated dependability and predictability — a partner's actions reliably matching their words. Rempel, Holmes & Zanna (1985) modeled trust as predictability + dependability + faith, and found these dimensions closely tied to love and satisfaction. Wieselquist et al. (1999) showed a 'mutual cyclical growth' loop: pro-relationship acts build the partner's trust and commitment, whereas broken commitments and self-serving behavior erode trust — which in turn withdraws the goodwill that sustains the relationship.",
