    description: "In self-determination theory, amotivation is the state of acting without intention or valuing — going through the motions with no 'why'. It is fed by frustration of the three basic psychological needs (autonomy, competence, relatedness). Meta-analysis across 99 work samples found need satisfaction robustly predicts engagement, performance, and well-being, while need frustration predicts burnout, low vitality, and ill-being; amotivation sits at the maladaptive pole of the motivation continuum with the poorest cognitive, affective, and behavioral outcomes.",
