    description: "Adaptive self-regulation requires knowing when to let go: disengaging effort and commitment from goals that have become impossible, and re-engaging with attainable ones. People who cannot disengage stay locked in hopeless pursuits, and Wrosch and colleagues link low goal-adjustment capacity to more depressive symptoms, higher perceived stress, elevated cortisol, and worse physical-health indicators; those who can disengage AND re-engage report the highest subjective well-being.",
