    description: "Self-concordance is the degree to which goals express one's authentic interests and values rather than external pressure or guilt. Sheldon and Elliot's longitudinal work shows a four-step path: low self-concordance predicts less sustained effort, which predicts lower attainment, less need satisfaction, and smaller well-being gains even when goals ARE reached. Pursuing goals for the 'wrong' reasons produces a fragile striving that fades under difficulty and yields hollow success.",
