    description: "BDD — distressing preoccupation with perceived appearance flaws — carries some of the highest suicidality in psychiatry. A meta-analysis (Angelakis et al., 2016) found people with BDD had ~3.8x the odds of suicidal ideation and ~2.6x the odds of a suicide attempt versus those without, with clinical samples reporting lifetime ideation near 78% and attempts near 24–28%. Sufferers withdraw socially, pursue repeated cosmetic procedures, and lose years to appearance-related rituals and avoidance.",
