    harm: { severity: 4, onset: "months", reversibility: "partial" },
    degrades: ["mental health", "career trajectory and job performance", "self-esteem", "sleep quality"],
    description: "Sustained mistreatment at work — persistent humiliation, exclusion, or intimidation — is meta-analytically tied to mental and physical health harm. Nielsen & Einarsen's (2012) review (Study 1: 137 effects, N=77,721) links exposure to depression, anxiety, burnout, PTSD symptoms, and turnover intent; Verkuil et al. (2015) confirmed the association in both cross-sectional and longitudinal data. A Nordic multicohort study (2023) found bullying associated with later suicide risk (HR 1.32, 95% CI 1.09–1.59).",
    callout: "Much of the evidence is self-report and cross-sectional, and the bullying-suicide link attenuated to non-significance (HR 1.16, 0.96–1.41) after adjusting for baseline mental health — prior distress both predicts and is worsened by bullying, so effects are partly bidirectional.",
