    degrades: ["sense of belonging", "self-esteem", "mood regulation", "perceived control and meaning"],
    description: "Being ignored and excluded — even briefly, even by strangers in the Cyberball ball-toss task — reliably threatens the four fundamental needs (belonging, self-esteem, control, meaningful existence). A meta-analysis of 120 Cyberball studies (N=11,869; Hartgerink et al., 2015) found a large, robust effect (d > |1.4|) that generalized across age, gender, and even when players knew the game was scripted. A single episode is largely transient, but chronic exclusion tracks with depression and worse health.",
    callout: "The popular 'social pain uses the physical-pain matrix' claim is contested: a meta-analysis of rejection imaging (Cacioppo et al., 2013) failed to confirm dACC/pain-matrix overlap, so the 'rejection literally hurts' framing is weaker than often stated.",
