    description: "Chronic failure to meet a child's emotional or physical needs is among the most damaging maltreatment subtypes, distinct from active abuse. Norman et al.'s (2012) systematic review found physical neglect roughly doubled the odds of depressive/anxiety disorders (OR ~2), and emotional neglect predicts the highest depression effect sizes of any maltreatment type in Childhood Trauma Questionnaire studies. Prevalence among adults with psychiatric disorders is high (~43% emotional, ~35% physical neglect). Effects persist into adulthood and predict a worse, more recurrent course of depression.",
