    description: "The systematic sweep of attention through the body (a core MBSR component) is often sold as a stress cure, but the dedicated meta-analysis (Gan et al., 2022) found no reliable benefit on clinical symptoms such as depression versus active or passive controls, only a small effect on trait mindfulness versus passive control. Its clearer signal is interoceptive: a separate 29-RCT meta-analysis (~2,191 participants) found small-to-medium gains in self-reported interoception from body-based mindfulness training. So the honest read is a body-awareness trainer, not a mood treatment.",
