    description: "The Synapse Project RCT (Park et al., 2014; N=221 older adults) randomized participants to learn a demanding, novel skill (digital photography, quilting, or both) ~15 hours/week for 3 months, versus social or low-demand conditions. Only the high-challenge groups improved episodic memory; the social and passive/receptive conditions did not, and some gains persisted at 1-year follow-up. Unlike abstract brain-training drills, real effortful skill acquisition showed durable memory benefit.",
