    description: "The claim that learning music 'makes you smarter' does not survive rigorous meta-analysis. Sala & Gobet (2020; 54 studies, 6,984 children) found that once study-design quality is controlled, the effect of music training on cognitive and academic skills is essentially null and highly consistent. Music training makes you better at music — it does not reliably raise IQ, memory, or academic achievement.",
