    description: "Economic theory (Yaari, 1965; Davidoff, Brown & Diamond, 2005, American Economic Review) shows guaranteed lifetime income has real welfare value as longevity insurance, income you cannot outlive. But that value applies mainly to simple single-premium immediate annuities (SPIAs); the far more heavily marketed variable and indexed annuities carry high fees, surrender charges, and complexity that erode the benefit. SPIAs are a tiny slice of sales (~3%), reflecting the 'annuity puzzle': under-use of the useful kind and over-sale of the costly kind.",
