    description: "The marshmallow test's fabled power to forecast a child's future was overstated. Watts, Duncan & Quan's 2018 conceptual replication (~900 children) found the age-4 delay to age-15 achievement correlation was about half the original and dropped by roughly two-thirds after controlling for family background and early cognition - an extra minute of waiting predicted only ~0.1 SD. Waiting is partly a rational read of whether the environment is reliable; 'cooling' strategies (distraction, reframing) and dependable follow-through help more than willpower drills.",
