    description: "Flow (deep, absorbed engagement) is not random: meta-analysis identifies challenge-skill balance, clear goals, and a sense of control as its most robust antecedents, meaning you can deliberately set up conditions that make flow likelier. Fong, Zaleski & Leach (2015), pooling 28 studies, found challenge-skill balance related moderately to flow (r roughly .2-.3), and a separate meta-analysis (Harris et al., 2021) links flow to better performance across domains. The practical lever is to pick tasks that stretch skill without overwhelming it, define the goal sharply, and build in fast feedback.",
