    feeds: ["creative problem-solving", "insight and restructuring", "breaking mental fixation"],
    description: "Setting a stuck problem aside and returning to it later reliably raises solution rates. Sio & Ormerod's (2009) meta-analysis found a positive incubation effect, strongest for divergent-thinking problems, larger after longer preparation, and reduced when the break is filled with a cognitively demanding task. Baird et al. (2012) sharpened this: an undemanding task during the break (which lets the mind wander) beat rest or hard work for improving performance on previously seen problems.",
