    description: "Adding poles turns walking into a whole-body exercise that recruits the upper body and raises aerobic demand without more perceived effort. A meta-analysis of RCTs in cardiovascular-disease patients found Nordic walking improved exercise capacity and dynamic balance, and in peripheral artery disease increased walking distance and oxygen uptake more than conventional care; in heart failure it raised peak VO2 by ~2.2 mL/kg/min. A separate meta-analysis of 22 studies (1,271 older adults) found improvements in BMI, cholesterol, triglycerides and systolic blood pressure. It is accessible, low-impact and well-suited to older or deconditioned people.",
