    feeds: ["(Investigational, unproven in healthy adults)", "Possible cardiometabolic effects (metformin, in diabetics)"],
    description: "The two most-hyped 'anti-aging' drugs remain investigational in healthy people. The TAME trial (metformin in non-diabetic elders) was designed with the FDA but has not reported healthy-human longevity results; observational and preclinical signals exist but are confounded. Rapamycin's PEARL RCT (114 adults, 1 year) was safe but MISSED its primary endpoint (visceral fat) and produced no lifespan evidence. Strong in mice, unproven in people.",
    callout: "Do not confuse animal data with human proof — no completed RCT shows either drug extends healthy lifespan in non-diseased people. Metformin may even blunt the mitochondrial and strength gains from exercise (Konopka 2019). Both carry real side-effect and off-label risks.",
