    degrades: ["Fairness in assigning blame (in negative-event contexts only)", "Empathy for others' situational constraints"],
    description: "The classic claim is that we explain our own behavior situationally ('I was stressed') but others' dispositionally ('she's just rude') — a built-in double standard that fuels conflict. Honesty demands the deflation: Malle's (2006) meta-analysis of 173 studies found the overall asymmetry is near zero (d ≈ -0.02 to 0.09), surviving only in narrow conditions (negative events, intimate targets, idiosyncratic actors). The intuitive 'we always excuse ourselves and judge others' story is largely a textbook myth.",
