    description: "Emotional reasoning, or ex-consequentia reasoning ('If I feel anxious, there must be danger'), is inferring objective threat from one's own anxious feelings rather than from evidence. Arntz, Rauner & van den Hout (1995) showed anxiety-disorder patients infer danger from their fear response even when objective information says it is safe, whereas non-anxious people infer danger only from the objective facts — fueling a vicious cycle of avoidance and maintained irrational belief.",
