    description: "A negotiator's Best Alternative To a Negotiated Agreement (BATNA) is the single most robust determinant of what they capture at the table. Across experimental dyads, negotiators with an attractive alternative extract systematically better deals, an effect mediated by perceived power, and it holds even for uncertain or purely 'phantom' alternatives. Entering without a cultivated alternative or a pre-set reservation point means no credible walk-away, so the counterpart controls the range and the negotiator settles near their own limit.",
