    description: "In the Vlaeyen–Linton fear-avoidance model, misinterpreting pain as a sign of danger drives avoidance of movement, which produces disuse, physical deconditioning, and disability — a self-reinforcing loop. Kinesiophobia affects an estimated 50-70% of chronic-pain patients, and fear-avoidance beliefs prospectively predict disability and work loss, especially in the transition from acute to chronic pain. Graded exposure/activity that breaks the avoidance loop improves function.",
