    description: "Horne's Necessity-Concerns Framework shows adherence is driven less by knowledge than by the balance of beliefs: how strongly a patient perceives the medicine as necessary versus their concerns about harms and dependence. A meta-analysis of 94 studies (~25,072 patients) found higher necessity beliefs (OR ≈ 1.74) and fewer concerns (OR ≈ 0.50) predicted better adherence across conditions. When concerns dominate, patients under-use effective treatment and disease progresses.",
