    degrades: ["seeing the ethical stakes of a decision in real time", "keeping stated values connected to actual behavior", "catching one's own slide before it compounds"],
    description: "Bounded ethicality is the systematic, non-conscious tendency to act against one's own values without noticing. 'Ethical fading' is the mechanism: when a choice is framed as a business, legal, or numbers problem, its moral dimension drops out of awareness, so people who genuinely believe they are ethical drift into wrongdoing (Challenger, Ford Pinto, mortgage-era misrepresentation). Because the harm is unintended and invisible to the actor, ordinary willpower and good-person self-image provide no protection — the danger is precisely that the person never 'decides' to be unethical.",
