    weakness: { threat: 6, weakLines: ["Meta-Cognitive", "Volitional"], degree: "major contributor", onset: "immediate", reversibility: "partial" },
    degrades: ["Vigilance / sustained attention", "Error avoidance in real time", "Safety-critical performance"],
    description: "A high propensity to mind-wander and slip into attention lapses raises error and accident risk in demanding real-time tasks. A case-control study of injured drivers (Galera et al., 2017, PLOS ONE) found that intense/disruptive mind-wandering just before a crash was associated with being the at-fault driver (roughly doubled odds). Overt digital distraction compounds this: Caird et al.'s (2014) meta-analysis of texting-while-driving showed degraded reaction time, eye movements, lane-keeping and detection.",
