    description: "A chronic prevention focus — vigilance about losses, rules, and avoiding errors — tends to steer people toward safe, incremental, loss-avoiding choices rather than the exploratory risk-taking that novelty requires. Promotion-focused people, by contrast, show more fluency and openness to novel stimuli. The honest picture is nuanced: some studies find prevention focus lowers creativity and raises risk aversion, but others find prevention-focused people match promotion-focused output on unmet goals and even produce more elaborated ideas.",
