    description: "Non-fatal drowning can leave survivors with hypoxic-ischemic (anoxic) brain injury whose severity tracks submersion time and resuscitation quality. The most vulnerable regions — hippocampus, basal ganglia, insular cortex — produce persistent memory, cognitive, and motor deficits, and after a significant hypoxic insult full recovery is not the norm. Coma length and functional status on admission are strong predictors of long-term outcome. Onset is immediate and severe injury is typically lasting.",
