    description: "Pain that outlasts the healing of an injury or surgery is common and disabling. A review of systematic reviews (Bansal et al., 2024) reports chronic post-surgical pain — new pain persisting ≥3 months without other cause — in roughly 10–50% of surgical patients, varying by procedure (e.g. ~15% pooled after spinal surgery, ~20% after bone/joint surgery). It frequently co-travels with persistent opioid use, mood disturbance, and sleep loss. Distinct from generic chronic pain in its clear injury/surgical onset and preventable component. Onset is over months; often lasting.",
