    description: "A compulsive drive to exercise despite injury, exhaustion, or life disruption. It is NOT a formal DSM-5 or ICD-11 diagnosis; it is measured by self-report scales (e.g., Exercise Addiction Inventory). A 2020 meta-analysis (13 studies, n=3635) found prevalence around 8.1% in general exercisers, 5.0% in amateur athletes, and 5.5% in students in the absence of eating-disorder symptoms, with higher rates in endurance/fitness contexts. Correlates include elevated anxiety, overtraining, overuse injury, and relative energy deficiency (RED-S).",
