    description: "Compulsive, non-specific overuse of the internet (beyond a single app or game) with loss of control and functional impairment. Only Internet Gaming Disorder appears in DSM-5 (Section III, research appendix); generalized PIU is not a recognized standalone diagnosis. A 2020 meta-analysis of 133 studies estimated a weighted prevalence of generalized internet addiction around 7.0%, and student meta-analyses report moderate positive associations with depression, anxiety, loneliness, and poor sleep.",
