    description: "Home dampness and visible mold are consistently associated with new-onset and worsened asthma, wheeze, cough, bronchitis, and upper-respiratory symptoms. A 2012 systematic review/meta-analysis (16 cohort/case-control studies) found dampness/mold present before disease onset significantly raised asthma-development risk; meta-analytic odds ratios typically show 30–70% higher prevalence of respiratory effects in damp/moldy homes. The Institute of Medicine and WHO reached concordant conclusions.",
