    description: "In the largest network meta-analysis ever run (Cipriani 2018: 522 trials, ~116,000 patients), all 21 antidepressants beat placebo for acute major depression, with odds ratios for response of roughly 1.5–2.1 and an overall standardized mean difference of about 0.30 — a real but modest effect. Benefit is clearest in moderate-to-severe depression and thinner in mild cases, where much of the response overlaps with placebo. SSRIs (sertraline, escitalopram) sit mid-pack for efficacy but rank well on tolerability, which is why they are first-line.",
