    description: "Periconceptional folic acid (400 mcg/day, higher for prior affected pregnancy) is one of the best-evidenced supplement interventions: RCT and umbrella-review data show roughly a 70% reduction in neural tube defects (pooled RR ~0.31-0.43), and it drove mandatory grain fortification worldwide. The deflation: its OTHER heavily-marketed uses are weak — folate/B-vitamins reliably lower plasma homocysteine but large RCTs and Cochrane reviews show that homocysteine lowering does NOT reduce heart attacks or (with rare stroke-subgroup exceptions) cardiovascular events or mortality.",
