    id: "iron-supplementation", section: "1305", title: "Iron — Deficiency Correction (and Over-Supplementation Harm)", subtitle: "practice: 'Bolsters clusters: Bodily, Meta-Cognitive, Emotional'",
    evidenceTag: "Strong",
    impact: { magnitude: 3, latency: "weeks", durability: "sustained", effort: "low" },
    feeds: ["Bodily", "Meta-Cognitive", "Emotional"],
    description: "For iron-deficiency anemia, oral iron reliably raises hemoglobin and relieves fatigue, and correcting deficiency improves cognition, exercise capacity and restless-legs symptoms; IV iron works faster where oral fails or is not tolerated. But iron is a double-edged mineral: supplementing people who are NOT deficient offers no benefit and carries harm — GI intolerance, and in genetic hemochromatosis or repeated transfusion, iron overload causes cirrhosis, cardiomyopathy and diabetes. Acute overdose is a leading cause of pediatric poisoning death.",
