    description: "B12 is essential for myelin, DNA synthesis and hematopoiesis; deficiency causes megaloblastic anemia and subacute combined degeneration of the cord. Correction is strongly beneficial in the genuinely deficient — vegans (no reliable plant source), older adults (food-cobalamin malabsorption, ~10-20% of elderly), metformin/PPI users, and post-gastrectomy. Oral high-dose is as effective as intramuscular for most. The crucial deflation: in older adults with mild/moderate deficiency but no symptoms, RCTs show no cognitive benefit from supplementation.",
