    description: "The classic Cochrane review is a model of honest deflation. Regular vitamin C supplementation does NOT prevent colds in the general population. It does modestly shorten them: routine >=0.2 g/day cut mean cold duration by about 8% in adults and 13% in children — roughly a fraction of a day. The one meaningful prevention signal is in people under extreme physical stress (marathon runners, soldiers, skiers), where regular vitamin C roughly halved cold incidence. Therapeutic dosing started after symptom onset showed no consistent benefit.",
