    description: "Factor-analysis of the Ruminative Responses Scale splits rumination into two subtypes: 'brooding' (moody, judgmental dwelling on 'why do I have problems?') and 'reflection' (purposeful, curious self-examination). Only brooding uniquely predicts higher depression one year later after controlling for baseline depression; reflection predicts higher concurrent but LOWER future depression, i.e. it can be protective. This is the honest correction to the flat claim that 'all self-focus is bad' — the maladaptive ingredient is the brooding factor specifically.",
