    description: "Post-event processing (PEP) is the after-the-fact, repetitive replay of a social encounter — dredging up one's own perceived flubs even after positive feedback. It is a distinct maintenance mechanism in Clark & Wells' model, separate from anticipatory worry or co-rumination. A 2024 systematic review and meta-analysis found a moderate association between PEP and social anxiety (r ≈ 0.45, 95% CI [0.40-0.50]), and PEP biases memory toward negative self-relevant details.",
