    degrades: ["sustained deliberation", "effortful self-control", "analytic engagement", "hard-goal pursuit"],
    description: "Given two options of equal payoff, people reliably pick the one that demands less mental work — mental effort carries an intrinsic subjective cost that discounts reward, independent of time or error rate. In Kool et al.'s six demand-selection experiments the bias held across settings; effort-discounting (COGED) work shows the cost is measurable and encoded in a valuation network. Chronic, trait-like effort avoidance predicts shallow engagement, dropped hard tasks, and reliance on heuristics over analysis.",
