    degrades: ["Emotional", "Intrapersonal", "Interoceptive", "Volitional"],
    description: "Emotional inertia is how strongly your feelings carry over moment-to-moment — measured as the autocorrelation of emotion across time. High inertia signals a system that fails to respond flexibly to changing context; it is elevated in low self-esteem, neuroticism and depression, and — importantly — prospectively predicts the onset of clinical depression in adolescents, beyond perseverative thinking. It captures a rigidity distinct from simple 'moodiness' or variability.",
