    description: "Without a transient to flag it (a flicker, blink, cut, or occlusion), people miss large changes to a scene. Simons & Levin's real-world study had an experimenter swapped for a different person mid-conversation during a brief occlusion — around half of people never noticed they were now talking to a stranger. The failure exposes how little of a scene we actually represent moment to moment and fuels misplaced confidence in memory and eyewitness accounts.",
