    description: "Disclosure normally builds liking, but Collins & Miller's (1994) meta-analysis shows the effect depends on appropriateness and reciprocity: too much, too soon, or one-sided disclosure signals intrusiveness and neediness rather than intimacy. Early over-disclosers are judged less mature and less well-adjusted (Wortman et al., 1976) and prompt unflattering attributions, so the oversharer repels the closeness they seek. It is the mirror-image failure of conversational under-disclosure/narcissism.",
