    description: "Kapur's productive failure has learners attempt to solve a novel problem BEFORE being taught the canonical method (problem-solving-then-instruction, PS-I). Even though their initial solutions usually fail, the struggle primes deeper understanding of the later explanation. Sinha & Kapur's meta-analysis (53 studies, 166 comparisons, >12,000 learners) found a moderate benefit over instruction-first (g ~0.36), rising to g ~0.37-0.58 with high-fidelity implementation, especially for conceptual and transfer outcomes.",
