    description: "Failing to correctly appraise and act on acute cardiac or neurological symptoms is directly lethal because reperfusion is time-critical. In acute MI, every 30-minute delay to reperfusion raises relative 1-year mortality ~7.5%, yet ~40% of patients have prehospital time over four hours. In stroke, only a minority reach hospital inside the 3-4.5-hour thrombolysis window — one cohort found a median prehospital delay of 11 hours and 91% of patients/relatives had never heard of FAST. This is a distinct, minutes-matter failure of bodily-signal appraisal, separate from general care-avoidance.",
