    description: "A climate of silence — shared belief that speaking up about problems is futile or dangerous — causes employees to withhold information about issues and errors. Managerial fear of negative feedback plus implicit beliefs that dissent is disloyal produce collective sensemaking that 'speaking up is unwise,' starving leaders of the very signals they need to correct course. Distinct from team-level psychological safety: this is an organization-wide climate that blocks change, error correction, and ethical challenge.",
