    degrades: ["Financial", "Mathematical", "Strategic"],
    description: "Beyond its useful budgeting form, mental accounting produces costly errors when people treat money in different 'accounts' as non-interchangeable: carrying high-interest credit-card debt while holding low-yield savings, splurging 'windfall' or tax-refund money differently from earned income, or protecting an untouchable savings jar while borrowing at 20%. Thaler's synthesis shows these patterns violate fungibility and can dominate optimal allocation. The strategic cost is capital that sits in the wrong pocket at the wrong price.",
