    degrades: ["Bodily", "Interoceptive", "metabolic regulation", "circadian alignment"],
    description: "Social jetlag — the habitual gap between the body clock and socially imposed sleep timing, measured as the shift in mid-sleep between work and free days — is a behavioral form of chronic circadian misalignment. It is associated with obesity, metabolic syndrome, type-2 diabetes and cardiometabolic risk markers, especially in evening chronotypes; a meta-analysis links evening chronotype and social jetlag to worse metabolic parameters in non-shift workers. Unlike imposed shift work, this misalignment is partly self-generated by inconsistent weekday/weekend schedules and late 'catch-up' sleep.",
