    description: "Habits are cued by stable contexts, so the most reliable window to break an unwanted one is when the context itself changes (moving house, new job, new city). Wood, Tam & Guerrero Witt (2005) tracked transferring students: exercise, TV and newspaper habits survived the move only when the old cues persisted; when context changed, behavior fell back under intentional control. Field experiments (Verplanken & Roy, 2016) show sustainability nudges land far harder on recent movers, and interventions timed to disruptions consistently outperform the same nudge in a stable setting.",
