    feeds: ["Financial", "Meta-Cognitive", "Volitional", "Systemic"],
    description: "Scheduling a recurring (annual or quarterly) review of net worth, allocation drift, contribution rates, insurance coverage, beneficiaries, and goal progress — a periodic audit distinct from continuous expense tracking. Its mechanism is progress monitoring: Harkin et al. (2016) meta-analysis (138 studies, N≈19,951) found interventions that increase monitoring of goal progress reliably raise attainment (d+ = 0.40), with larger effects when progress is physically recorded or made public.",
