    impact: { magnitude: 2, latency: "months", durability: "sustained", effort: "moderate" },
    feeds: ["Financial", "Moral", "Strategic", "Existential"],
    description: "Concentrating several years of charitable gifts into one tax year (often via a donor-advised fund, then granting out over time) so total itemized deductions clear the standard-deduction threshold. After the 2017 TCJA roughly doubled the standard deduction, fewer households itemize, raising the after-tax 'price' of giving. Meer & Priday (2020) estimate a tax-price elasticity of giving and project TCJA-driven reductions; bunching is the behavioral workaround for donors who still want the deduction.",
