    feeds: ["Financial", "Systemic", "Strategic", "Volitional"],
    description: "Staggering maturities (e.g., CDs or Treasuries maturing in years 1-5) so a portion matures each period and is reinvested. The structure diversifies reinvestment/interest-rate risk across time: if rates rise, maturing rungs reinvest at higher yields; if they fall, longer rungs stay locked. It sits between a single bullet maturity and formal duration-immunization (Bierwag, Kaufman & Toevs, 1983) as a simple, rules-based way to fund near-term cash needs.",
