    description: "In isolated/idiopathic RBD the normal paralysis of REM sleep fails, so people physically enact dreams — punching, kicking, leaping — injuring themselves and bed partners. Its deeper cost is prognostic: pooled longitudinal data estimate phenoconversion to an overt synucleinopathy at roughly 31% by 5 years, 60% by 10 years, and ~73% by 12 years. Conversion is most often to Parkinson's disease (~44%) or dementia with Lewy bodies (~25%), making iRBD one of the strongest known prodromal markers of neurodegeneration; anosmia and constipation raise the risk further.",
