    description: "A distinct acute chemical pneumonitis (not nicotine dependence): in the 2019-2020 US outbreak, 2,807 hospitalizations and 68 confirmed deaths were reported to CDC. Vitamin E acetate — a diluent added to illicit THC vaping cartridges — was found in bronchoalveolar-lavage fluid of 48 of 51 patients but none of healthy controls, implicating it as the primary cause. Presentation includes dyspnea, cough, fever, GI symptoms and hypoxemia; ~86% of cases involved THC-containing products and patients skewed young (median age 24) and male (~67%). Survivors can be left with persistent reduced diffusing capacity.",
