    description: "Spasticity — velocity-dependent muscle overactivity after upper-motor-neuron injury — develops in roughly a quarter of stroke survivors (pooled prevalence ~25.3%), and in ~40% of those with first-ever stroke and paresis. It restricts range of motion and produces abnormal postures, pain, and difficulty with dressing, hygiene, and transfers; people with spasticity report worse physical functioning, more pain, and lower vitality. Left untreated it drives muscle shortening, fibrosis, and fixed contractures that compound disability.",
