    description: "Narcolepsy (prevalence ~0.03–0.067%, often type 1 with orexin/hypocretin loss and cataplexy) causes irrepressible daytime sleep attacks, disrupted night sleep, and — in type 1 — sudden loss of muscle tone triggered by emotion. Health-related quality of life and physical performance are markedly below normative values, with impairment across academic, occupational, and social domains. Observational and real-world (CV-BOND) data show elevated cardiovascular and cardiometabolic comorbidity, including a high burden of hypertension and loss of nocturnal blood-pressure dipping, a pattern linked to excess mortality in the general population.",
