    description: "Myalgic encephalomyelitis/chronic fatigue syndrome is a real, disabling illness — worldwide prevalence near 1% — whose hallmark is post-exertional malaise: a delayed, disproportionate worsening of symptoms after minor physical or mental effort. Disability is severe: roughly 25–29% of patients are house- or bedbound, unemployment estimates run from ~35% to ~69% (a Spanish community study found 58.6% unemployed), and U.S. societal costs are estimated at $17–24 billion annually. Functional impairment is described as comparable to heart disease or multiple sclerosis.",
