    degrades: ["Balance & Spatial Confidence", "Work Capacity", "Emotional Stability", "Mobility", "Quality of Life"],
    description: "PPPD (defined by the Bárány Society in 2017, now in ICD-11) is chronic non-spinning dizziness, unsteadiness, and sensitivity to motion and complex visual environments, typically persisting ≥3 months and often triggered by an acute vestibular event. It is predominantly seen in women and middle age. Patients show significantly higher Dizziness Handicap Inventory scores and poorer quality of life than people who recover from acute vestibular episodes, with high rates of comorbid anxiety and depression; longer illness duration further increases anxiety and physical handicap.",
