    harm: { severity: 3, onset: "months", reversibility: "partial" },
    degrades: ["Pain-Free Function", "Autonomic Regulation", "Sleep", "Sensory Comfort", "Quality of Life"],
    description: "Small-fiber neuropathy selectively damages thinly-myelinated and unmyelinated fibers, producing burning/stabbing distal pain, temperature and pin-prick loss, and autonomic symptoms (palpitations, GI disturbance, orthostatic dizziness) — often with normal nerve conduction studies, so it is under-recognized. A large population study put minimum prevalence near 53 per 100,000. It is a well-defined chronic painful condition causing severe individual burden and reduced quality of life; roughly half of cases are idiopathic, with diabetes, autoimmune disease, and post-viral triggers among identified causes.",
