    degrades: ["Bodily", "Interoceptive"],
    description: "The dose-response for exercise and the heart is J/U-shaped: moderate activity is strongly protective, but decades of high-volume endurance training carry a paradoxically elevated atrial-fibrillation risk. Meta-analysis finds roughly a 5-fold higher AF odds in endurance athletes versus controls, driven by left-atrial enlargement, fibrosis and vagal tone. Lifelong very-active male athletes also show higher coronary-artery-calcium scores, though the plaque tends to be more stable/calcified. This is distinct from overtraining syndrome or low-energy-availability (RED-S): it is a structural cardiac adaptation of the highest-volume athletes.",
