    degrades: ["Spatial", "Mathematical", "Mechanical"],
    description: "Mental rotation and spatial visualization are among the most predictive-yet-neglected cognitive abilities for technical careers. Wai, Lubinski & Benbow's (2009) analysis of >400,000 people over 50 years showed adolescent spatial ability forecasts STEM degree completion and career entry over and above math and verbal ability — so weak spatial skill quietly filters people out of engineering, chemistry, and surgery. It also slows acquisition of skills that require imagining objects in 3D (e.g., laparoscopy, mechanical assembly).",
