    description: "Loss or weakness of smell is an underrated sensory deficit with outsized life consequences. People with anosmia are about three times more likely to experience a hazardous event (undetected gas, smoke, spoiled food), lose eating pleasure leading to poor nutrition and weight change, and show markedly elevated depression and social isolation. Strikingly, Pinto et al. (2014) found olfactory dysfunction predicts 5-year mortality in older adults — anosmics had over 3× the odds of death (OR ≈ 3.37) independent of major disease, making smell one of the strongest single mortality markers studied.",
