    description: "Garfinkel's dimensional model separates interoceptive accuracy (objective performance, e.g., heartbeat detection), sensibility (self-reported attentiveness), and awareness (the match between them). A large gap — believing you read your body well while performing poorly — yields a high 'interoceptive trait prediction error' that predicts greater anxiety. This is distinct from alexithymia/somatization: it is a mis-calibration of body-signal reading, not amplified symptom reporting.",
