    description: "Ideational flexibility — the ability to break set and move across conceptual categories — is a distinct executive contributor to creative output, separate from the mechanized 'Einstellung' mindset. People who cannot shift set tend to perseverate within one category, producing many same-flavor ideas (high fluency, low flexibility) and missing the remote combinations that read as original. Executive-function studies (e.g., Benedek et al.) show updating and shifting jointly support divergent thinking, and weak shifting predicts lower originality.",
