    weakness: { threat: 5, weakLines: ["Creative", "Pattern-Recognition"], degree: "major contributor", onset: "months", reversibility: "partial" },
    degrades: ["Creative", "Pattern-Recognition", "Entrepreneurial"],
    description: "Divergent-thinking (DT) fluency — how many usable ideas you can generate — is the most-studied index of creative potential, and low fluency prospectively forecasts thin creative achievement. Kim's (2008) meta-analysis and Said-Metwaly et al.'s (2022) updated meta-analysis both find a statistically reliable DT→achievement link, but the pooled correlation is modest (roughly r ≈ .2), so weak fluency is a real drag rather than a death sentence. DT scores have predicted teacher-rated creativity and creative activity years later, meaning the deficit shows up downstream, not just on the test.",
