    description: "In Blascovich's biopsychosocial model, appraising a demanding task as a threat (demands > resources) rather than a challenge (resources > demands) yields maladaptive cardiovascular reactivity (vasoconstriction, lower cardiac output) and typically poorer performance. A meta-analysis of cardiovascular markers (Behnke & Kaczmarek, 2018) found challenge states facilitate performance but with small, publication-bias-affected effects.",
