    degrades: ["Adversarial", "Social-Perceptual", "Emotional", "Meta-Cognitive"],
    description: "Anxious individuals selectively orient attention toward threatening stimuli. Bar-Haim et al.'s (2007) meta-analysis of 172 studies (~4,000 participants) found a reliable threat bias in anxiety (d ≈ 0.45) absent in non-anxious people. The bias taxes working memory, distorts risk perception, and keeps the system scanning for danger instead of pursuing goals.",
