    description: "People default to presuming honesty (Levine's Truth-Default Theory). Bond & DePaulo's meta-analysis of 206 studies (~24,000 judges) found average deception-detection accuracy is only 54% — barely above chance — with a strong truth bias and near-zero benefit from expertise. Over-reliance on this default, plus faith in nonverbal 'tells' that don't work, leaves goals exposed to con artists.",
