    description: "Detached mindfulness (Wells) means noticing a trigger thought while deliberately withholding any further coping, analysis, or worry in response — observing the thought as a passing mental event with no engagement. It is theoretically distinct from ACT cognitive defusion (which alters the thought's literal grip) and from mindfulness meditation (which cultivates present-moment attention): the target is stopping perseverative processing. Metacognitive therapy built around it shows large effects for GAD and depression (MCT meta-analytic g's often >1.0).",
