    degrades: ["Bodily", "Emotional", "Volitional", "Interoceptive"],
    description: "Karasek's demand–control model predicts that jobs combining high psychological demands with low decision latitude ('high strain') raise cardiovascular risk. The IPD-Work consortium's pooled analysis of ~197,000 workers across 13 European cohorts found job strain carried an age/sex-adjusted hazard ratio of 1.23 (95% CI 1.10–1.37) for incident coronary heart disease. This is a real but modest effect — the population-attributable risk was ~3.4%, far smaller than smoking. It is distinct from unemployment or burnout: the harm is chronic exposure to demand without control while still employed.",
