    description: "Distinct from base-rate neglect: when new evidence arrives, people revise their probability estimates in the right direction but by far less than Bayes' theorem prescribes — often updating only a fraction of the warranted amount. Phillips & Edwards demonstrated this 'conservatism' in the simplest possible two-hypothesis task, and it has recurred in 100+ experiments since. It leaves diagnosticians and forecasters chronically under-reactive to informative data.",
