    description: "Sticky capital and headcount budgets — allocating roughly what each unit got last year regardless of shifting opportunity — is a quiet but costly strategic failure. Firms that actively reallocate resources toward higher-return units create substantially more value than 'peanut-buttered,' inertial allocators; reallocation inertia grows with size, unrelated diversification, and HQ detachment. The bottleneck to strategy is often not knowing what to do but being unable to move money and people to it.",
