    description: "Distinct from simply misreading a fair graph: this is being actively deceived by manipulated ones. Pandey et al. showed that common distortions — truncated y-axes, exaggerated aspect ratios, area-scaling, inverted axes — measurably shift viewers' conclusions in the intended misleading direction. Truncating an axis reliably inflates the perceived size of a difference. Weak resistance here makes a person easy to steer with 'chartjunk,' cherry-picked baselines, and dual-axis tricks.",
