    feeds: ["Rhetorical", "Adversarial", "Strategic", "Interpersonal", "negotiation"],
    description: "An extreme first request that is refused, followed immediately by a smaller real request, raises compliance through reciprocal concession and perceptual contrast. Meta-analyses (O'Keefe & Hale 2001, odds-ratio; Feeley, Anker & Aloe 2012, first 35 years) find a reliable small-to-moderate effect that is strongest when the same person makes both requests, the cause is prosocial, and there is no delay between requests.",
