    description: "Secure agreement on attractive terms, then reveal added costs only after the person has committed; the commitment tends to hold. Cialdini, Cacioppo, Bassett & Miller (1978) demonstrated it across three experiments, and a later meta-analysis (Pascual et al.) found it reliably increases compliance. It works through commitment/consistency once the person has psychologically 'owned' the decision.",
