    description: "A single, named, identifiable person elicits more helping and donation than statistics about many. Small, Loewenstein & Slovic (2007) showed people give more to an identifiable victim than to statistical victims — and that prompting deliberation shrinks this gap. Note the broader 'vividness effect' (that vivid beats pallid information at persuading) is only weakly supported; Taylor & Thompson (1982) found it surprisingly elusive.",
