    description: "Messages arousing fear about a threat can shift attitudes, intentions, and behavior — but chiefly when paired with clear efficacy (a concrete action plus belief that it works). Tannenbaum et al.'s (2015) meta-analysis (248 samples, 27,372 people) found a small positive average effect (d≈0.29) with little evidence of backfiring, strongest when self- and response-efficacy are provided; Witte & Allen (2000) reach the same efficacy conclusion.",
