    description: "Handgrip strength is a cheap, whole-body vitality gauge: low grip robustly predicts all-cause and cardiovascular mortality, disability and future frailty, independent of muscle mass. Meta-analysis of ~3 million people found lowest-versus-highest grip carried HR ~1.41 for all-cause and ~1.63 for cardiovascular mortality; in the PURE study each 5-kg decrement raised all-cause mortality HR ~1.16 and cardiovascular mortality HR ~1.17 — a stronger death predictor than systolic blood pressure. It marks risk earlier and more distinctly than the full frailty phenotype.",
