    description: "Interpretation bias is the tendency to resolve ambiguous situations, faces, or sentences in a threatening/negative direction — a cognitive vulnerability distinct from attentional bias to threat. Experimental cognitive-bias-modification (CBM-I) studies show interpretation can be causally trained: modifying it changes anxiety reactivity, supporting a causal (not merely correlational) role. Effect sizes on the bias itself are large (g ≈ 0.81) but downstream clinical symptom effects are small (g ≈ 0.17-0.32), so it is a genuine but modest maintaining mechanism.",
