    description: "Resistance to peer influence rises roughly linearly from ~age 14 to 18, so early-to-mid adolescents are developmentally least able to say no to peers. Steinberg & Monahan (2007), pooling >3,600 individuals aged 10-30, found little growth in this capacity before 14 or after 18. Low resistance predicts susceptibility to antisocial peer pressure, delinquency, substance use and risky driving, and is amplified when peers are physically present.",
