    degrades: ["Rhetorical", "Interpersonal", "Strategic", "Intrapersonal"],
    description: "Doing good work is necessary but not sufficient — decision-makers reward the contributions they can see. Chronic under-claiming (excessive modesty, refusing to make one's competence legible) suppresses competence ratings and hireability. Rudman (1998) showed self-effacement lowered perceived competence and hireability for men, and that self-promotion raised competence ratings; the field-level meta-analysis (Ng et al., 2005) finds 'organizational sponsorship' and visibility variables predict promotion and salary. The honest asymmetry: the same self-promotion that helps agentic candidates triggers social-likability backlash for women, so the fix is not simply 'brag more.'",
