    weakness: { threat: 5, weakLines: ["Bodily", "Spatial"], degree: "moderate contributor", onset: "years", reversibility: "partial" },
    degrades: ["Bodily", "Spatial"],
    description: "Simple and choice reaction time — and especially its intra-individual variability — is a sensitive marker of central nervous-system integrity that predicts death and accidents. In NHANES-III, each SD of slower reaction time raised all-cause mortality HR ~1.25 and cardiovascular mortality ~1.36; in a 17-year cohort, greater reaction-time variability independently predicted mortality beyond dementia, age and CV risk. Slowed and variable responding also underlies driving-crash and workplace-error risk in aging and fatigue.",
