    degrades: ["Bodily", "Interoceptive"],
    description: "Poor endurance and control of the trunk extensors and deep core musculature is a modest prospective risk factor for first-episode and recurrent low back pain, not merely a consequence of it. In previously pain-free people, low trunk-extensor endurance has been associated with roughly 3-fold higher odds of developing low back pain, and poor lumbopelvic control predicts injury in athletes. Core-stability training reliably improves trunk endurance and reduces pain and disability in chronic low back pain, though usually no better than general exercise.",
