    description: "Failing to build a high-quality relationship with one's own boss ('managing up') leaves an employee in the low-exchange out-group: fewer resources, weaker ratings, less latitude. Dulebohn et al.'s (2012) meta-analysis of 247 studies found leader-member-exchange (LMX) quality is shaped partly by follower behaviors (competence, affect, contribution) and mediates key outcomes including performance, satisfaction, and turnover. Neglecting the upward relationship is thus a controllable career weakness, not just the boss's fault.",
