    weakness: { threat: 4, weakLines: ["Bodily", "Volitional"], degree: "moderate contributor", onset: "years", reversibility: "recovers" },
    degrades: ["Bodily", "Volitional"],
    description: "In Stodden's developmental model, weak fundamental motor competence (throwing, catching, running, jumping) launches a negative spiral: the low-skilled child perceives themselves as physically incompetent, withdraws from play and sport, gains less fitness, and falls further behind — a reciprocal loop that widens with age. Meta-analysis confirms a positive motor-competence-to-fitness relationship strengthening across childhood into early adulthood, and low motor competence tracks toward greater sedentary behavior and higher weight status.",
