    description: "Intimacy grows through a reciprocal process of disclosure met by responsiveness; chronic under-disclosure — emotional guardedness, never revealing inner states — starves that process. Longitudinal couple data show self-disclosure is positively associated with relationship satisfaction, love and commitment over time, and links to relationship esteem and perceived partner responsiveness. This is the opposite pole of the already-catalogued 'oversharing': too little disclosure keeps bonds shallow, blocks partners from knowing and supporting you, and reads as coldness or distrust.",
