    description: "Deep-but-narrow skill that is specific to one firm or niche is less transferable and commands less of a market premium at the top. Custódio, Ferreira & Matos (2013), building a general-skills index from the résumés of S&P 1,500 CEOs, estimated a ~19% pay premium for generalist over specialist CEOs (~$1M/year), largest when firms hire externally or face complex tasks like restructurings and M&A. Over-specialization also raises obsolescence and single-employer lock-in risk.",
