    description: "Teasing works only when both parties recognize the 'off-record' playful frame; when the target misses it, prosocial teasing reads as hostility. People chronically over-estimate how clearly their humor, sarcasm and teasing come across: across five experiments senders predicted ~97% comprehension of sarcastic/serious intent but achieved ~84% — an egocentric blind spot that is worse over text, where paralinguistic cues vanish. Conceptual reviews show identical teasing can bond or wound depending on delivery and status; miscalibrators repeatedly bruise relationships while believing they were 'just joking'. This is distinct from a trait aggressive humor style — it is a metacommunication error.",
