    description: "Standardized do-verify checklists for high-stakes procedural execution (distinct from checklists for one-off decisions). Haynes et al. (2009) reported the 19-item WHO Surgical Safety Checklist cut death from 1.5% to 0.8% and complications from 11% to 7% across eight global hospitals. Checklists offload memory, force communication, and catch skipped steps under pressure.",
