    description: "Learners alternate tutor and tutee roles, so each teaches and is taught. Distinct from being a mentor (long-term, one-directional) and from peer instruction lectures. Leung's (2019) meta-analysis found peer tutoring benefits the tutor's own achievement (weighted d approximately 0.43), and higher-education meta-analyses report moderate gains in course performance for both roles — teaching to learn, empirically confirmed.",
