    id: "microlearning", section: "1965", title: "Microlearning (Short, Focused Bursts)", subtitle: "practice: 'Bolsters clusters: Meta-Cognitive, Linguistic'",
    evidenceTag: "Emerging",
    impact: { magnitude: 2, latency: "weeks", durability: "sustained", effort: "low" },
    feeds: ["Meta-Cognitive", "Linguistic", "Logical"],
    description: "Delivering content in short (roughly 5-10 minute), single-objective units, often on mobile and spaced across days. Recent higher-education meta-analyses report positive effects on retention (pooled OR approximately 1.87) and learning outcomes (SMD approximately 0.74), plausibly because short units cut extraneous cognitive load and force repeated retrieval.",
