    description: "People preferentially seek, weight, and remember evidence that fits a favored hypothesis and under-test it against disconfirming cases — a 'positive test strategy.' From Wason's rule-discovery task onward, this is one of the most robust findings in reasoning research. A meta-analysis of selective exposure found a reliable preference for attitude-consistent information (d ≈ 0.36), the search-side engine of belief entrenchment and blind spots.",
