    description: "Trust is adaptive on average, but a dispositional propensity to trust that is not updated by trustworthiness cues (ability, benevolence, integrity) leaves people open to exploitation. A meta-analysis of 162 replications of the investment/trust game (>23,000 participants) shows trusters routinely send resources that a self-interested counterpart can simply keep; a separate meta-analytic model (132 samples) distinguishes trust propensity from perceived trustworthiness and links miscalibration to risk-taking that predicts worse outcomes. The failure is not trusting, but trusting indiscriminately.",
