    description: "When clots after a pulmonary embolism fail to dissolve, they can organize into fibrotic obstructions that drive progressive pulmonary hypertension and right-heart failure — a distinct disease from primary pulmonary arterial hypertension. CTEPH develops in roughly 3–4% of acute PE survivors and, untreated, brings breathlessness, exercise collapse and poor survival. It is one of the few 'curable' pulmonary hypertensions: pulmonary endarterectomy yields ~91% one-year and ~65% five-year survival from diagnosis, though ~25% retain residual PH.",
