    harm: { severity: 4, onset: "years", reversibility: "partial" },
    degrades: ["Bodily", "Emotional", "Financial", "Interoceptive", "Volitional"],
    description: "When chronic lung disease (most often COPD) raises pulmonary artery pressure, the right ventricle strains and eventually fails — cor pulmonale. Up to ~20% of COPD patients show right-ventricular dysfunction, and its presence predicts more hospitalizations and worse survival; classic figures put ~30% five-year survival once cor pulmonale is established in COPD. It marks a transition from lung disease to combined cardiopulmonary decline, distinct from primary pulmonary arterial hypertension.",
