    degrades: ["Bodily", "Linguistic", "Spatial", "Meta-Cognitive", "Emotional"],
    description: "Narrowing of the carotid artery is a largely asymptomatic reservoir of stroke risk that is distinct from stroke itself. On modern intensive medical therapy the annual ipsilateral stroke rate for severe asymptomatic stenosis is low (~1–2%), but the threatened event — disabling stroke with language, spatial and cognitive loss — is what gives the condition its weight. Symptomatic (post-TIA) stenosis carries markedly higher short-term stroke risk.",
    callout: "Educational, not medical advice. Because medical therapy has improved, the absolute benefit of endarterectomy/stenting for asymptomatic stenosis is now small and debated (CREST-2); routine revascularization for asymptomatic disease is no longer automatic and carries its own peri-procedural stroke risk.",
