    description: "Trait anhedonia — a stable deficit in anticipating or consuming reward and a chronically low positive-affect set point — is distinct from active dampening of good moods and from momentary sadness. Anhedonia symptoms in youth prospectively predict later onset of depression, and across psychiatric samples anhedonia predicts suicidal ideation even after controlling for overall depression severity, marking it as a partly independent risk pathway (blunted reward/positive-valence system).",
