    degrades: ["Emotional", "Intrapersonal", "Interoceptive", "Meta-Cognitive"],
    description: "Emotion granularity is the ability to represent feelings with specificity ('let-down and resentful' rather than a blurry 'bad'). People low in emotion differentiation regulate worse: a meta-analysis of clinical and non-clinical samples tied low differentiation to greater behavioral dysregulation (binge drinking, aggression, self-harm), and low granularity is over-represented in depression, anxiety, eating disorders, and borderline personality disorder. It is conceptually distinct from alexithymia (which is failure to identify/describe feelings at all) — granularity is about the resolution of an emotion vocabulary a person can otherwise access.",
