    description: "RESE (Caprara & Gerbino) is the perceived capability to manage despondency/distress and anger/irritation and to express positive emotion — a Bandurian self-efficacy applied to affect, distinct from NMR outcome-expectancies. Low RESE is associated with anxiety, depression, and externalizing problems; longitudinal work across countries links low self-efficacy for regulating sadness and anger to later internalizing and externalizing maladjustment, and Caprara found RESE beliefs help counteract depression and delinquency in late adolescence.",
