    description: "Radically Open DBT frames a distinct failure mode opposite to the usual under-control story: chronic OVER-regulation — rigid behavior, perfectionism, inhibited emotional expression, and detail-focused processing that produces loneliness and social isolation. Overcontrol is theorized to underlie treatment-refractory depression, anorexia nervosa, and obsessive-compulsive personality traits. In the RefraMED randomized trial (n=250) RO-DBT reduced depressive symptoms at 7 months versus treatment-as-usual, though the advantage was not statistically significant at 12 and 18 months.",
