    description: "Within alexithymia, the Toronto Alexithymia Scale separates Difficulty IDENTIFYING Feelings (DIF) from Difficulty DESCRIBING Feelings (DDF) — and the two carry different consequences. DDF specifically predicts interpersonal problems: it independently forecasts low agency AND low communion on the Inventory of Interpersonal Problems even after controlling for negative affect, because putting feelings into words is how people create closeness and steer others. This is the distinctly interpersonal, expressive facet of alexithymia, separable from the somatization pathway usually tied to DIF.",
