    description: "Non-hormonal lubricants (used at the time of sex) and regular vaginal moisturizers (used every few days for baseline symptom control) reduce dryness and painful intercourse from the genitourinary syndrome of menopause and other causes. A 2024 systematic review concluded moisturizers may improve dryness and, to a lesser extent, dyspareunia; they are recommended first-line, low-risk options and can be combined with hormonal therapy.",
