    degrades: ["Emotional", "Intrapersonal", "Parental", "Social-Perceptual", "Volitional"],
    description: "Postpartum psychosis is a rare, rapid-onset emergency (roughly 1–2 per 1,000 births) appearing days to weeks after delivery, with confusion, mania, delusions and hallucinations — often bizarre and infant-focused. A Swedish cohort of 1.6 million women recorded it in about 0.15% of first childbirths. It carries markedly elevated risks of suicide and infanticide (older estimates around 5% and up to ~4% respectively in untreated cases) and strong familial loading (sibling relative recurrence ~10.7). With prompt treatment prognosis is generally good, which makes recognition the whole game.",
    callout: "Absolute infanticide/suicide risk figures come from older and small case series and vary widely; modern treated outcomes are far better. It is a medical emergency requiring urgent psychiatric care — not something to manage at home. Educational, not medical advice.",
