    description: "Acute stress disorder (ASD) is the intrusion, avoidance, arousal and dissociation seen in the first days-to-month after trauma. Its clinical cost is dual: acute functional collapse (sleep loss, hypervigilance, dissociation, impaired return to work) and its role as a marker for later PTSD. Bryant's systematic review found ASD has reasonable positive predictive power — most people with ASD go on to PTSD — but poor sensitivity, because the majority who eventually develop PTSD did NOT meet full ASD criteria acutely. Peritraumatic dissociation is among the strongest single predictors of chronic PTSD.",
