    description: "A large share of well-formulated strategies fail not in logic but in follow-through — the translation from vision into coordinated day-to-day action breaks down. Sull, Homkes & Sull's multi-year survey work locates the failure in weak cross-unit coordination and inability to reallocate resources, NOT (contrary to lore) in weak alignment to the top. Common execution killers include competing initiatives for finite capacity and follow-through that dissolves once attention moves on.",
