    weakness: { threat: 5, weakLines: ["Strategic", "Volitional", "Meta-Cognitive"], degree: "moderate contributor", onset: "months", reversibility: "recovers" },
    degrades: ["Strategic", "Volitional", "Meta-Cognitive"],
    description: "Declaring a long list of 'top' priorities spreads finite attention and resources so thin that none get the focus needed to succeed — a failure of ranking, not effort. Execution research repeatedly flags 'too many competing initiatives for finite capacity' as a leading cause of strategy failure, and strategy scholarship converges on a small handful (roughly 3-5) of genuine priorities as the practical ceiling. The mechanism overlaps operational WIP overload but here it is decision-level: refusal to say no.",
