    degrades: ["Symptom stability", "Functional baseline", "Activity pacing", "Recovery trajectory"],
    description: "In fatigue- and pain-dominated chronic illness (ME/CFS, long COVID, chronic low-back pain), a common maladaptive pattern is overactivity-on-good-days followed by a crash — the 'boom-bust' cycle. In pain, Hasenbring's avoidance-endurance model identifies dysfunctional endurance/overactivity (pushing through, task persistence, thought suppression) as a driver of overuse strain and long-term disability, contrasting with the fear-avoidance pole. In post-exertional-malaise conditions, repeated overexertion beyond one's energy limit is associated with a progressively lower functional baseline. This is a distinct interoceptive self-regulation weakness, not athletic overtraining.",
