    degrades: ["Social-Perceptual", "Interpersonal", "Leadership"],
    description: "Cultural intelligence (CQ) is the capability to function effectively across cultures, spanning motivational, cognitive, metacognitive, and behavioral facets. Low CQ shows up as misreading norms, mistiming directness and hierarchy cues, and failing to adjust behavior — producing awkwardness, offense, blown negotiations, and failed expatriate or multicultural-team collaborations. Rockstuhl & Van Dyne's (2018) bifactor meta-analysis links CQ to cultural adjustment and to task, citizenship, adaptive, and leadership performance, with motivational CQ especially predicting socially oriented outcomes and metacognitive CQ predicting intercultural judgment. In a globalized, multicultural workplace, weak CQ is a distinct interpersonal liability separate from general social skill.",
