    description: "The interpersonal circumplex predicts 'complementarity': smooth interactions tend to mirror on warmth (warmth invites warmth) and oppose on dominance (one person's assertiveness invites the other's deference, and vice-versa). People who miscalibrate — meeting dominance with counter-dominance (escalating power struggles) or answering warmth with coldness — generate friction, lower rapport, and rejection. Sadler, Ethier & Woody's real-time dyadic studies show partners naturally adjust warmth and dominance in complementary ways, and dyads that complement on warmth like each other more and perform tasks faster and more accurately. Chronic anti-complementary behavior (rigid over-dominance or rigid over-submission) is a distinct social-perceptual weakness from low warmth alone.",
