    impact: { magnitude: 2, latency: "days", durability: "transient", effort: "low" },
    feeds: ["Volitional", "Rhetorical", "Strategic"],
    description: "Higgins' regulatory-fit theory: motivation and felt value rise when the way you pursue a goal matches your orientation — eager, gain-seeking means for a promotion focus; vigilant, loss-avoiding means for a prevention focus. Field studies matching health messages to a person's chronic focus raised screening, sunscreen and dietary intentions/behaviour, and fit reliably intensifies engagement and 'feeling right' about a pursuit.",
