    description: "Ascaris, hookworm, and Trichuris infect on the order of 1.5 billion people (about a quarter of humanity), concentrated in the poorest regions, causing anemia, undernutrition, and stunting in children. But the honest finding is that large Cochrane reviews of mass community deworming show little or no effect on average weight, hemoglobin, cognition, or school performance — a major challenge to the long-standing 'deworm-to-boost-learning' narrative. The direct morbidity is real; the population-level cognitive/economic payoff of mass treatment is not well supported.",
