    weakness: { threat: 3, weakLines: ["Spatial"], degree: "major contributor", onset: "immediate", reversibility: "recovers" },
    degrades: ["Map comprehension", "Map-to-terrain translation", "Route planning", "Reading relief/scale/orientation"],
    description: "Map-reading is a learnable skill distinct from real-world navigation ability: it requires translating a symbolic 2D representation (including relief/hypsography and scale) into ground truth, and people differ widely in it. Studies of navigational map reading find that map-related abilities and prior map experience are the strongest predictors of performance, while error analyses show novices fail most on wayfinding tasks that demand mental rotation and reading terrain relief. Weak cartographic literacy produces systematic map misinterpretation — misjudging distance, orientation, and which real-world feature a symbol denotes.",
