    description: "Fluid or pus in the pleural space — distinct from parenchymal lung disease. Malignant pleural effusion (MPE) complicates about 15% of cancers (lung, breast, lymphoma, mesothelioma) and signals advanced disease: 30-day mortality ~37% and 1-year mortality ~77%, with median survival typically 3-12 months. Empyema (infected pleural collection) carries 30-day/1-year mortality around 11%/26%, rising to ~30-50% in ICU patients. Both cause disabling breathlessness and repeated drainage procedures.",
