    description: "A collapsed lung from air leaking into the pleural space, typically in tall, thin young smokers (primary spontaneous pneumothorax; annual incidence ~18-28/100,000 men, ~1.2-6/100,000 women). The core cost is recurrence: a systematic review/meta-analysis of ~13,500 patients found pooled 1-year recurrence ~29% and overall ~32% after a first episode, dropping to ~10% after video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery. Recurrences cause acute breathlessness, repeated procedures, activity/flying/diving restrictions, and anxiety.",
