    degrades: ["Meta-Cognitive", "Logical", "Social-Perceptual", "Street-Smarts"],
    description: "An availability cascade is a self-reinforcing spiral in which a risk claim, once expressed, gains plausibility purely through repetition and rising visibility in public discourse. Kuran & Sunstein show two engines: informational (people infer truth from others' apparent belief) and reputational (people publicly echo the claim to stay socially accepted, silencing doubts). Individuals susceptible to cascades adopt whatever fear is currently amplified, driving public panics, mispriced risks, and costly over-regulation of minor hazards while genuine threats are ignored.",
