    description: "Much charitable giving is driven by the 'warm glow' of having donated rather than by the marginal good the donation does. Andreoni's impure-altruism model formalizes this selfish-satisfaction component; because warm glow is roughly insensitive to effectiveness, donors spread money thinly, ignore that top charities can be 100x more cost-effective than average ones, and react to salient overhead figures rather than outcomes. Caviola and colleagues document 'impact neglect,' scope insensitivity, and overhead aversion as systematic barriers to effective giving.",
