    degrades: ["Strategic", "Systemic", "Volitional", "Adversarial"],
    description: "Facing a multi-front risk, people take one salient protective action, feel their worry discharged, and then stop — even when the single action barely dents the threat and several more are needed. Weber documented this for farmers, climate risk, and health: buying one insurance policy, installing one device, or making one green purchase reduces felt anxiety and creates an illusory sense of adequate protection. The emotional relief, not the actual risk reduction, terminates the behavior, and moral-superiority feelings can even spill over into reduced further effort.",
