    description: "How you select people is one of the best-evidenced management levers. Schmidt & Hunter's (1998) synthesis of 85 years of data put structured interviews at validity .51 (vs .38 unstructured) and work-sample tests among the strongest predictors of job performance; structuring means standardized questions and anchored scoring rubrics. Structured methods also reduce the halo, similarity, and first-impression biases that plague free-form interviews.",
