    description: "CAH from 21-hydroxylase deficiency (>95% of cases) affects ~1 in 10,000-20,000 births. The classic salt-wasting form presents in the neonatal period with hyponatremic dehydration and adrenal crisis that is fatal if untreated; before newborn screening, deaths were documented (a German survey recorded 14 deaths 1973-2004, none after screening improved). Lifelong glucocorticoid ± mineralocorticoid replacement is required, and after adrenal crisis, cardiovascular events are the second leading cause of death.",
