    description: "Primary aldosteronism is the commonest endocrine cause of secondary hypertension — present in ~5-15% of hypertensives (up to ~14% of newly diagnosed) and ~5.8% of stroke/TIA patients — yet it is grossly underdiagnosed. Compared with BP-matched essential hypertension it independently raises stroke (OR ~2.6), atrial fibrillation (OR ~3.5), coronary disease (OR ~1.8), and heart failure. It is one of the few surgically or medically curable causes of resistant hypertension, so missing it is a large, modifiable harm.",
