    degrades: ["Meta-Cognitive", "Creative", "Intrapersonal"],
    description: "Cryptomnesia is unconscious plagiarism: a previously encountered idea resurfaces feeling brand-new and self-generated, a specific source-monitoring failure. Brown & Murphy's group generation-and-recall paradigm showed 3-9% of the time participants either replicated another person's item or claimed another's idea as their own; in some conditions the majority plagiarized at least once. It rises when the original source is low-salience, when ideas are elaborated, and under cognitive load — a real risk for anyone doing collaborative creative or research work.",
