    description: "Forming an intention to exercise is a weak predictor of actually exercising. In Rhodes & de Bruijn's meta-analysis (2013) using the action-control framework, about half of people who intended to meet activity guidelines failed to do so, while almost none of the non-intenders became active — the gap is overwhelmingly 'inclined abstainers,' people who mean to but don't. Intention explains only a modest share of activity variance; the rest is post-intentional (habit, self-regulation, opportunity).",
