    description: "People — especially those with obesity — systematically underreport how much they eat and overestimate how much they move, and they often genuinely believe their reports. Lichtman et al.'s landmark doubly-labeled-water study (1992, NEJM) found 'diet-resistant' subjects who reported eating <1200 kcal/day were actually underreporting intake by ~47% and overreporting physical activity by ~51%; their metabolism was normal. This measurement failure quietly sabotages self-directed weight goals: the interoceptive/self-monitoring signal people trust is biased.",
