    description: "In defined-contribution plans, many savers simply split contributions roughly evenly across whatever funds are offered — the '1/N heuristic' — so the equity share of a portfolio is driven by the fund menu rather than by any risk preference. Adding one more stock fund to a plan mechanically pushes participants toward more equity; adding a bond fund pushes them the other way. Allocation becomes an artifact of menu design instead of a deliberate risk decision.",
