    description: "A transactive memory system (TMS) is a team's shared map of 'who knows what' — its specialization, credibility, and coordination. When TMS fails to develop (churn, siloing, no shared task history), members duplicate work, fail to route problems to the right expert, and re-decide from incomplete facts. Reviews find TMS reliably and positively predicts team performance (correlations commonly around r ≈ .30–.40 across dozens of studies), so its absence is a real, if moderate, drag on collective output.",
