    description: "About 410,000 people developed multidrug- or rifampicin-resistant TB in 2022, yet the global treatment-success rate was only ~63% (up from ~50% a decade earlier) and roughly 20% of those started on treatment die during it. Outcomes are worse still for extensively drug-resistant (XDR) TB. Even 'cured' patients often carry permanent post-TB lung damage, and legacy regimens meant 18-24 months of toxic drugs.",
