    degrades: ["Moral", "Volitional", "Meta-Cognitive"],
    description: "Unethical behavior rarely arrives full-blown; it ramps. Welsh, Ordóñez, Snyder & Christian (2015), across four experiments, found people who commit a minor infraction (padding an expense, a small lie) become markedly more willing to commit larger ones later — because a slowly rising baseline never triggers the moral alarm a single big jump would. Small, easily-rationalized steps launder later big ones. This is the mechanism behind most 'how did it get this far' corporate and personal collapses.",
