    degrades: ["Moral", "Community", "Social-Perceptual"],
    description: "Human moral enforcement is parochial: people will pay a personal cost to punish unfairness and reward fairness, but disproportionately in favor of their own ethnic, language, or group members. Bernhard, Fischbacher & Fehr (2006), using third-party punishment games with indigenous Papua New Guinea groups, found altruistic norm enforcement was strongly biased by group membership. Choi & Bowles (2007) modeled how in-group altruism and out-group hostility could have co-evolved through intergroup war. The failure mode: 'justice' that is genuine but caps at the tribe boundary, licensing indifference or harm to outsiders.",
