    description: "Morphological analysis decomposes a problem into independent parameters, lists options for each, and systematically combines across them to cover the full solution space. In a controlled study of 102 first-year engineering students (Daly et al.), morphological analysis and Design Heuristics produced significantly higher concept elaboration than individual brainstorming — though plain brainstorming produced the most concepts in a 25-minute session and diversity did not differ. Its strength is exhaustive coverage and building-out of ideas, not raw volume.",
