    impact: { magnitude: 2, latency: "weeks", durability: "transient", effort: "moderate" },
    feeds: ["Creative", "Entrepreneurial", "Strategic", "Interpersonal"],
    description: "Design thinking frames ideation inside an empathize–define–ideate–prototype–test loop, using structured prompts (constraints, 'yes-and', reverse-ideas) to expand options before converging. Roth et al. (2020) provided the first quantitative evidence that higher application of design-thinking practices predicts better project performance, and Casper, Helminen & Veinott's (2024) experiment found resource-constraint plus 'yes-and' prompts generated 64% more ideas (though not more original ones), while a reverse-ideas lateral-thinking prompt roughly doubled original ideas. Overall the empirical base is still small and much of the popular literature is consultancy hype.",
