    weakness: { threat: 5, weakLines: ["Creative", "Interpersonal", "Intrapersonal", "Rhetorical"], degree: "moderate contributor", onset: "immediate", reversibility: "recovers" },
    degrades: ["idea expression", "creative risk-taking", "candor in groups"],
    description: "Fear of being judged makes people withhold their more unusual ideas in the moment. Camacho & Paulus (1995) showed a stable individual difference: people high in interaction/social anxiousness generated markedly fewer ideas when brainstorming face-to-face than when working alone, whereas low-anxious people were relatively unaffected — the anxious members drag interactive-group output down. The apprehension acts as a self-imposed filter that removes exactly the risky, original ideas ideation is meant to surface.",
