    feeds: ["Bodily", "Volitional", "Intrapersonal"],
    description: "Automated SMS/text reminders cue a target behavior (taking medication, attending appointments) at the point of action. Thakkar et al.'s meta-analysis found text messaging roughly doubled the odds of medication adherence in chronic disease (rates ~50% to ~68%). But design matters sharply: a meta-analysis of one- vs two-way messaging found one-way reminders had little effect (RR ~1.04) while two-way (reminder + reply) improved adherence ~23% (RR ~1.23).",
