    id: "regret-lottery-incentives", section: "2892", title: "Regret Lotteries / Lottery-Based Incentives", subtitle: "practice: 'Bolsters clusters: Deposit Contracts & Loss-Framed Incentives, Financial Incentives for Behavior Change, Commitment Devices / Precommitment'",
    evidenceTag: "Moderate",
    impact: { magnitude: 3, latency: "weeks", durability: "transient", effort: "moderate" },
    feeds: ["Volitional", "Financial", "Intrapersonal"],
    description: "Instead of a fixed reward, participants enter a daily/weekly lottery but only collect winnings if they hit their behavioral target — exploiting regret aversion and overweighting of small probabilities. In Volpp et al.'s 16-week RCT the lottery arm lost ~13.1 lb vs ~1.8 lb in controls (deposit-contract arm ~14.0 lb), and ~53% hit the 16-lb goal vs ~11% of controls. The signature weakness is durability: weight was substantially regained after incentives stopped, though incentive groups still weighed less at 7 months than baseline.",
