    description: "Consumer step-counters/fitness bands (Fitbit-style) provide continuous self-monitoring plus goals. Brickwood et al.'s meta-analysis found trackers meaningfully increased physical activity (notably daily step count) in healthy adults, but trackers used alone produced effects roughly 50% smaller than multifaceted programs that added coaching or goal-setting. A recurring, honest limitation across reviews is engagement decay — effects tend to shrink as novelty wears off.",
