    weakness: { threat: 6, weakLines: ["Leadership", "Interpersonal", "Emotional"], degree: "major contributor", onset: "months", reversibility: "partial" },
    degrades: ["subordinate initiative", "self-esteem", "helplessness resistance", "unit climate", "voice"],
    description: "Ashforth's 'petty tyrant' lords power over subordinates through arbitrariness, self-aggrandizement, belittling, a forcing conflict style, discouraging initiative, and non-contingent punishment. The consequences he documents include lowered self-esteem, reduced work effort, heightened frustration/stress, and learned helplessness among subordinates. The construct spans more than personal abuse — the 'discouraging initiative' and 'arbitrariness' elements specifically kill the voluntary problem-solving that goals depend on.",
