    degrades: ["contact with reward/reinforcement", "behavioral activation / drive", "goal-directed activity", "mood"],
    description: "The behavioral model of depression (Ferster; Lewinsohn) frames low mood as a product of low response-contingent positive reinforcement plus negatively-reinforced avoidance: withdrawal gives short-term relief, which strengthens more withdrawal, which cuts off reward and deepens depression. Carvalho and Hopko show avoidance's link to depression is mediated by reduced positive reinforcement. Behavioral activation, which reverses the loop by scheduling reward-rich activity, is among the best-supported depression treatments, confirming the mechanism.",
