    feeds: ["Bodily", "Meta-Cognitive", "Intrapersonal"],
    description: "Watching edited video of oneself performing a skill correctly (positive self-review or feedforward) can accelerate acquisition and self-efficacy. The strongest quantitative evidence is in skill-teaching for autistic and disabled learners, where meta-analyses report large effects for functional-living and job skills (Tau-U ~0.83; ES ~0.85-0.95). Positive self-review tends to outperform feedforward editing.",
