    description: "Chronic use of vibrating power tools (grinders, chainsaws, jackhammers, riveters) causes HAVS: episodic finger blanching (vibration white finger), numbness, and reduced grip. A systematic review/meta-analysis found vibration-exposed workers carry roughly a 4-7-fold increased risk of Raynaud's phenomenon and neurosensory injury, with neural damage often appearing at shorter latency than vascular effects. In exposed groups such as vehicle mechanics, ~24% report cold-induced white finger and ~25% persistent numbness. It is distinct from whole-body vibration (which drives low-back pain).",
