    description: "Autosomal-recessive deficiency of the branched-chain alpha-ketoacid dehydrogenase complex lets leucine and its ketoacids accumulate to neurotoxic levels, causing the characteristic sweet-smelling urine, cerebral edema, coma, and death within 7-10 days of birth in untreated classic disease. Worldwide incidence is ~1 in 185,000 (far higher in some founder populations). A meta-analysis found newborn screening raised mean IQ (95 vs 82) and cut mortality (~3% vs ~15%) versus symptomatic detection. Lifelong protein-restricted diet is the mainstay; liver transplantation halts crises but cannot reverse prior brain injury.",
