    weakness: { threat: 6, weakLines: ["Strategic", "Meta-Cognitive", "Logical"], degree: "major contributor", onset: "years", reversibility: "partial" },
    degrades: ["Strategic", "Meta-Cognitive", "Logical"],
    description: "Tetlock's 20-year study of ~284 experts making ~28,000 political and economic predictions found their accuracy on multi-year events only marginally beat chance and often lost to simple statistical baselines. Worse, confidence was inversely related to accuracy: the most famous, most certain 'hedgehog' experts (one big theory) were the least accurate; humble, eclectic 'foxes' were better calibrated. Domain expertise did not confer forecasting skill.",
