    degrades: ["Pattern-Recognition", "Logical", "Adversarial"],
    description: "Dror and colleagues (2006) gave fingerprint experts prints they had previously matched, now framed with a misleading context (e.g., 'the suspect confessed to a different crime' or has an alibi). Experts reversed a substantial share of their own prior identifications — flipping match/no-match judgments based purely on irrelevant context. This shows that even feature-based expert perception is not context-immune, undermining assumptions of forensic objectivity.",
