    description: "Precrastination is the tendency to hasten completion of a subgoal even at the cost of extra effort, so as to offload it from memory. In Rosenbaum et al.'s bucket experiments, participants reliably picked up the nearer bucket and carried it farther than necessary — choosing more physical work just to 'start' sooner. Applied to knowledge work this shows up as answering trivial items immediately, replying before thinking, or doing low-value tasks first because holding them 'to do' feels aversive; the well-sequenced, higher-value path is sacrificed to discharge cognitive load.",
