    description: "Overdiagnosis — labeling a condition that would never have caused symptoms or death — turns healthy people into patients and triggers a cascade of tests, procedures, and treatments that can only harm. Roughly 15–30% of imaging and 20–40% of CT scans reveal incidental findings, and over 99% of physicians report cascades after incidentalomas. It is a real, systematically under-recognized iatrogenic harm, well documented for thyroid, prostate, breast, and lung screening.",
