    callout: "The two headline findings diverge largely because of how each handled reverse causation and smoking: restricting to healthy never-smokers (as Di Angelantonio did) removes much of the paradox, suggesting it is partly confounding artifact. Severe obesity's mortality risk is robust; overweight/grade-1 remains genuinely debated. Educational, not medical advice.",
