    id: "guided-play-learning", section: "3171", title: "Guided Play (Adult-Scaffolded Playful Learning)", subtitle: "practice: 'Bolsters clusters: Linguistic, Spatial, Creative'",
    evidenceTag: "Moderate",
    impact: { magnitude: 2, latency: "weeks", durability: "sustained", effort: "moderate" },
    feeds: ["Linguistic", "Spatial", "Creative", "Mathematical", "Volitional"],
    description: "A middle path between didactic instruction and free play: the child leads playful activity while an adult gently scaffolds toward a learning goal. Skene et al.'s 2022 meta-analysis (17 studies, N≈3,900, ages 1-8) found guided play outperformed direct instruction on early maths (g=0.24), shape knowledge (g=0.63), and task-switching (g=0.40), and beat free play on spatial vocabulary (g=0.93). Benefits were domain-specific, not across-the-board.",
