    description: "Fatigue is among the most common and disabling symptoms of multiple sclerosis, often ranked by patients as their single worst symptom and a major driver of unemployment. A 2024 meta-analysis (69 studies, 27 countries) estimated global MS-fatigue prevalence at 59.1%, consistent with an earlier review's 36.5–78% range. It is more frequent with greater disability, longer disease duration, and older age, and is partly independent of relapses — a persistent background burden even in otherwise stable disease.",
