    description: "CIPN is a dose-limiting, often painful sensory neuropathy from platinum agents, taxanes, vinca alkaloids, and bortezomib, presenting as glove-and-stocking numbness, tingling, and burning. A landmark meta-analysis (31 studies, 4,179 patients) found prevalence of about 68% in the first month after chemotherapy, ~60% at 3 months, and ~30% at ≥6 months — meaning a substantial minority are left with chronic, sometimes permanent, deficits. It frequently forces chemotherapy dose reduction, directly trading cancer control against neurotoxicity.",
