    description: "Burning mouth syndrome is a chronic intraoral burning or dysaesthesia lasting >2 hours daily for >3 months, with a clinically normal mucosa and no identifiable cause — now viewed as a neuropathic/nociplastic orofacial pain. A 2022 systematic review and meta-analysis found a pooled general-population prevalence of 1.73% (7.72% in clinical samples), with strong female predominance (1.15% women vs 0.38% men) and rising prevalence after age 50, peaking in women in the sixth-to-seventh decade. Regional estimates vary widely (Asia 1.05% vs Europe 5.58%).",
