    description: "Setting your own costly, spaced deadlines rather than cramming exploits the fact that people recognize their present bias and will pay to constrain it. In Ariely & Wertenbroch's classic experiments, students who self-imposed evenly spaced deadlines performed better than a single-final-deadline group, and many chose to bind themselves. The honest limit: self-set deadlines beat none but underperform externally imposed, evenly spaced deadlines because people set them suboptimally.",
