    description: "First described in animals by Dugatkin, mate-choice copying appears in humans: a person's desirability rises simply because others (especially attractive same-sex peers) are seen choosing them. A 2018 systematic review and meta-analysis found a reliable overall effect, robust for women evaluating men, weaker/mixed for men. As a decision failure it outsources judgment to social proof, inflating attraction to a partner on borrowed signal rather than genuine compatibility or safety.",
