    description: "If the harm is content, not screen time, changing WHAT is in the feed is the lever. Experiments show idealized/appearance-ideal images acutely raise body dissatisfaction and appearance comparison, while body-diverse or 'Instagram-vs-reality' content reduces it — implying that replacing idealized accounts with realistic/diverse ones should help. Following appearance-focused accounts correlates with more body surveillance and thin-ideal internalization. Distinct from time-based caps: this is content curation.",
