    description: "Distinct from scheduled notification-batching: this is turning alerts off. A within-subjects study (N=221) found a week of keeping notifications ON and the phone in reach raised inattention and hyperactivity symptoms versus a notifications-off week — implying the off-condition helps. But the 'Do-Not-Disturb Challenge' (N=30, 24 h notifications-off) showed the trade-off honestly: people felt less distracted and more productive, yet more anxious and less socially connected, and many could not sustain it. So the attentional upside is real but comes with social-responsiveness costs.",
