    description: "Rationing exposure to negative news (fixed windows, fewer check-ins) targets a documented acute effect: a classic experiment showed a 14-min negatively-valenced news bulletin raised anxious and sad mood AND increased catastrophizing of unrelated personal worries versus neutral/positive bulletins. Ecological-momentary work replicates that perceived-negative news predicts more negative and less positive affect day-to-day, moderated by personal relevance. Limiting intake is a low-cost lever against this; it is adjacent to but narrower than generic notification-batching.",
