    description: "Digoxin inhibits the myocardial Na+/K+-ATPase, causing bradyarrhythmias, ectopy, and — in acute overdose — hyperkalemia, which is the key prognostic marker. In the classic Bismuth series (pre-antidote era), serum potassium <5.0 mEq/L carried 0% mortality versus 100% at >5.5 mEq/L. Toxicity is disproportionately a disease of the elderly (the large majority of cases are >65) and of narrow-therapeutic-index dosing with renal impairment or drug interactions. Digoxin-specific antibody fragments (Fab; e.g., DigiFab), FDA-approved since 1986, bind and neutralize digoxin and markedly reduce mortality in life-threatening poisoning.",
