    description: "Serotonin syndrome is a predictable, dose-related toxidrome of excess serotonergic activity — a triad of neuromuscular hyperactivity (clonus, hyperreflexia, rigidity), autonomic instability, and altered mental status. It arises from therapeutic serotonergic drugs, overdose, or interactions (e.g., SSRIs with MAOIs, tramadol, linezolid). The Hunter Serotonin Toxicity Criteria (clonus-centered) have ~84% sensitivity and ~97% specificity. Most cases are mild and resolve with withdrawal of the offending agent plus supportive care and benzodiazepines; severe cases with hyperthermia can be life-threatening and may warrant cyproheptadine and aggressive cooling. US surveillance recorded tens of thousands of SSRI exposures with dozens of deaths in a single year.",
