    description: "Leverage is the mechanism that converts an ordinary loss into ruin: it magnifies gains and losses symmetrically while adding fixed debt-service and margin-call obligations that force selling at the worst time. Mian & Sufi show highly leveraged households drove the largest consumption collapses and default spikes of 2007-09, with home-equity borrowing fueling both the debt run-up and the wave of defaults. When entrepreneurs sign personal guarantees, business failure pierces into personal bankruptcy. Lusardi & Tufano find low debt literacy strongly predicts over-indebtedness and paying needlessly high borrowing costs.",
