    description: "The most reliable overt signature of marital distress is not just how much negativity a couple shows but their tendency to answer a partner's negativity with negativity — tit-for-tat escalation. Distressed couples show higher conditional probability of reciprocating anger/contempt, and this reciprocity is more stable across situations than raw negative-behavior counts. Woodin's meta-analysis found hostility robustly (medium effect) tied to lower satisfaction.",
