    description: "The classic 'bend the knees, keep the back straight' training is near-universal in workplaces, yet the largest Cochrane review (9 RCTs, ~20,101 workers, plus 9 cohorts) found NO evidence that manual-handling advice, training, or assistive devices prevent back pain or back-pain-related disability versus no intervention or minor advice. It is a genuinely distinct practice from job design, and the honest verdict is that technique training alone is one of ergonomics' best-studied disappointments.",
