    description: "Disorders of arousal from NREM sleep (confusional arousals, sleepwalking, sleep terrors) involve incomplete awakening from deep sleep with complex, amnestic behavior. They are common and usually benign in children (sleepwalking ~14.5%) but affect ~1.5-4.2% of adults, where they are less benign: three clinical studies found 31-54% of adult sleepwalkers/sleep-terror patients had injured themselves (fractures, lacerations, burns, concussion). Sleep-related violence was reported in ~1.6% of a general sample, and roughly a third of those reporting violent nocturnal behavior caused significant harm to self or others.",
