    description: "Sleep-related hypermotor epilepsy (SHE), formerly nocturnal frontal-lobe epilepsy, is a focal epilepsy of brief, stereotyped nocturnal seizures with asymmetric tonic/dystonic posturing or complex hyperkinetic behavior, often with retained awareness. Estimated minimum prevalence is ~1.8 per 100,000, and it accounts for roughly 10% of drug-resistant surgical epilepsy. Its overlap with NREM parasomnias is a major clinical cost: one large cohort reported a mean diagnostic delay of ~12.8 years in over half of cases, with parasomnia being the most frequent misdiagnosis (~55.5%), delaying antiseizure treatment.",
