    description: "Delayed sleep-wake phase disorder (DSWPD) is a chronic circadian misalignment in which endogenous sleep timing is shifted markedly late, so patients cannot fall asleep or wake at socially required times, producing weekday sleep deprivation, absenteeism and impaired concentration. Prevalence estimates cluster around ~1-4.5% in adolescents and young adults (with wider ranges of 1-16% across methods). A 2025 systematic review and meta-analysis found a significant association between DSWPD and depression in young people, alongside high rates of anxiety, ADHD and substance use.",
