    description: "Idiopathic hypersomnia (IH) is a rare central disorder of hypersomnolence marked by excessive daytime sleepiness despite normal or long sleep, severe sleep inertia ('sleep drunkenness') and daytime cognitive dysfunction. Population prevalence estimates are very low and imprecise (roughly 0.002-0.01%, with a 'probable IH' figure of ~1.5% in the objectively tested Wisconsin Sleep Cohort). It is a diagnosis of exclusion that overlaps heavily with narcolepsy type 2, producing diagnostic delays reported up to ~9 years, and it carries a high burden: reported work absenteeism (~12.3%) exceeded that seen in narcolepsy trials (~6.1%).",
