    description: "Nightmare disorder is defined by repeated, well-remembered, distressing dreams that impair functioning; while occasional nightmares affect up to ~45% of adults, the clinical disorder affects ~4%. It is heavily enriched in trauma populations (nightmares in ~50-90% of PTSD) and rises to ~16.7% in major depressive episodes. Importantly, nightmares are an independent risk factor for suicidal ideation and behavior beyond depression severity. Evidence-based treatment is effective: Imagery Rehearsal Therapy and exposure-based CBT reduce nightmare frequency, severity and distress, and prazosin is used for PTSD-related nightmares.",
