    description: "PLMD is defined by repetitive limb movements (PLMS) that fragment sleep with cortical micro-arousals, distinct from restless legs syndrome (which is a waking sensory urge). PLMS are uncommon before 40 but reach ~30% or more of adults over 50, and each event can drive discrete surges of roughly 20 mmHg in blood pressure and ~10 bpm in heart rate via sympathetic activation. Large cohorts have linked a high PLMS index to incident cardiovascular disease and mortality, and some data associate it with elevated dementia risk, though disentangling PLMS from comorbid OSA, RLS and age is difficult.",
