    description: "Therapeutic radiation can cause delayed harm years after treatment: progressive tissue fibrosis (skin, lung, fascia, bowel) and radiation-induced second cancers. In a SEER cohort of ~647,000 adult 5-year survivors, about 9% developed a second solid cancer but only an estimated 8% of those were attributable to the radiotherapy itself—roughly 5 excess cancers per 1,000 patients treated at 15 years for the higher-risk sites. Radiation fibrosis typically emerges 6 months to several years post-treatment and tends to be progressive and irreversible.",
