    description: "Emotional exhaustion — depletion of emotional and energetic resources — is the central, best-validated dimension of the Maslach Burnout Inventory and the one most strongly tied to job demands. In Alarcon's (2011) meta-analysis across ~230 samples, exhaustion showed the strongest links to workload/demands and to intent-to-leave; both demand and resource correlates related more strongly to exhaustion than to the other two dimensions (Lee & Ashforth, 1996). It is the 'engine failure' that most directly stalls goal pursuit.",
