    description: "Siegrist's model holds that high effort met with low reward — poor pay, insecurity, thwarted recognition or promotion — creates a failed-reciprocity stress state distinct from Karasek's demand-control model. In the IPD-Work multicohort study of 90,164 workers, effort-reward imbalance predicted incident coronary heart disease over ~10 years (HR ≈ 1.16, 95% CI 1.00-1.35), and it consistently forecasts burnout, depression, and quitting. The chronic sense of unrewarded effort saps the will to keep investing in a goal.",
