    description: "Emotional labor is regulating one's felt emotions to meet display rules at work; 'surface acting' — faking or suppressing feeling without changing it — creates emotional dissonance. Hülsheger and Schewe's (2011) meta-analysis of 95 studies found surface acting reliably linked to emotional exhaustion, depersonalization, psychological strain, and lower job satisfaction, whereas 'deep acting' (actually shifting the felt emotion) was far less costly. Sustained surface acting bleeds the emotional resources goal pursuit relies on.",
