    description: "Cue-exposure therapy (CET) repeatedly presents drug/alcohol cues without consumption to extinguish conditioned craving. Meta-analytic reviews find real but limited effects on alcohol outcomes — often no better than standard CBT — largely because extinction learned in the clinic does not transfer to other contexts (the 'renewal effect'). Multi-context exposure and pairing CET with urge-specific coping skills improve durability.",
