    degrades: ["survival", "transplant outcomes", "functional independence", "bodily reserve", "immune function"],
    description: "Muscle wasting in cirrhosis (distinct from age-related sarcopenia) affects about 41% of patients and is driven by hyperammonemia, impaired protein synthesis, and hypermetabolism. It roughly doubles mortality risk (pooled HR ~2.1-2.6) independent of MELD, with waitlist-mortality HR ~1.7 and post-transplant HR ~1.8, plus more infections, longer ICU stays, and surgical complications. Because MELD misses it, sarcopenia is increasingly proposed as an add-on risk marker.",
