    description: "Hepatic hydrothorax is a transudative pleural effusion (usually right-sided) from ascitic fluid crossing diaphragmatic defects, occurring in about 5-16% of cirrhotics. It is now recognized as an independent decompensating event: median survival is roughly 8-12 months and 5-year survival ~15% versus ~31% without it. Diuretics alone achieve durable resolution in only ~12%; refractory cases need thoracentesis, TIPS, or transplant, and chest-tube drainage carries high complication rates.",
