    description: "Non-malignant portal vein thrombosis has a pooled prevalence of ~14% in cirrhosis (rising from ~1% in compensated disease to 8-25% in transplant candidates), with an annual incidence around 10%. Beyond complicating transplant surgery and raising variceal-bleeding risk, PVT tracks worse survival. The IMPORTAL competing-risk meta-analysis found anticoagulation reduced all-cause mortality (adjusted subdistribution HR 0.59, 95% CI 0.49-0.70) independent of recanalization, and without a clear excess of bleeding.",
