    description: "Distinct from dose-dependent acetaminophen toxicity, idiosyncratic DILI is an unpredictable reaction to therapeutic doses of drugs, supplements, and herbals, with population incidence around 14-19 per 100,000 person-years. In prospective registries about 5-10% of patients die within 6 months (roughly half liver-related) and ~4-5% require transplant; idiosyncratic reactions account for 13-17% of all acute liver failure. Hepatocellular injury with jaundice (Hy's law) carries ~10% mortality. Most cases resolve on withdrawal of the culprit, but a minority progress to chronic injury or failure.",
