    description: "CT-PTSD, derived from Ehlers & Clark's cognitive model, targets the sense of 'current threat' by updating trauma appraisals, discriminating triggers, and reducing maladaptive coping — distinct from Resick's Cognitive Processing Therapy in its idiographic memory-updating focus. Across seven RCTs it produced large PTSD reductions with unusually low dropout (~3% in the flagship trial). It is a NICE-recommended first-line trauma-focused therapy.",
