    description: "Popular claims that specific wall colors reliably control emotion or behavior are largely unsupported. The famous 'Baker-Miller / drunk-tank pink' calming effect (Schauss) was never fully replicated, and any effect fades within 15-30 minutes. Sweeping 'each color has a fixed emotion' schemes are marketing folklore. What survives is weaker and conditional: brightness/saturation and warm-vs-cool tone can nudge arousal and perceived room temperature, and effects interact with task and person — but hue-specific personality claims should be treated as near-null.",
