    description: "Conscientiousness — being organized, prudent, self-disciplined, reliable — is one of the most consistent personality predictors of longer life. A meta-analysis of 20 samples (>8,900 people; Kern & Friedman) found it reliably predicted lower mortality, with the more conscientious living roughly 2-4 years longer. The eight-decade Terman cohort showed conscientiousness rated by teachers in childhood (1922) still predicted survival decades later.",
