    description: "The fall in heart rate in the first minute after stopping exercise reflects vagal (parasympathetic) reactivation. Cole 1999 (NEJM, ~2,400 adults) found a first-minute drop of ≤12 bpm roughly doubled 6-year mortality, independent of fitness, medications and imaging. Later pooled data (>40,000 people) associate poor recovery with ~60-70% higher all-cause mortality. It is a nearly free autonomic-health readout you can track with a watch, and it improves with aerobic training.",
