    description: "Counting how many times you rise from a chair in 30 seconds (no arms) indexes lower-limb muscle power, which declines faster than strength with age. In the Toledo Study for Healthy Aging (~1,900 older adults), low relative sit-to-stand power was linked to substantially higher mortality (men with low power ~57% higher all-cause death risk) and to frailty and mobility disability. It is the trainable capacity behind the sit-to-rise and balance markers, and progressive/power-oriented resistance training improves it within weeks.",
