    feeds: ["Bodily", "cardiovascular recovery", "autonomic down-regulation"],
    description: "A narrative review (Van Hooren & Peake 2018, Sports Medicine) concludes active cool-downs are largely ineffective for the outcomes people expect: they do not meaningfully reduce next-day muscle soreness, markers of muscle damage, stiffness or range-of-motion loss, and do not prevent injury or blunt training adaptation. The honest upside is narrow — faster recovery of the cardiovascular/respiratory system and possibly reduced acute immune dip. Tapering rather than stopping abruptly is reasonable, but expect little DOMS relief.",
