    id: "tragic-optimism-las", section: "3739", title: "Tragic Optimism (Meaning Amid Suffering)", subtitle: "practice: 'Bolsters clusters: Existential, Emotional, meaning-under-adversity'",
    evidenceTag: "Emerging",
    impact: { magnitude: 2, latency: "months", durability: "sustained", effort: "moderate" },
    feeds: ["Existential", "Emotional", "meaning-under-adversity", "acceptance"],
    description: "Frankl's 'tragic optimism' — saying yes to life despite pain, guilt, and death — was operationalized by Wong and measured with Leung et al.'s 36-item Life Attitudes Scale (courage before adversity, self-transcendence, affirmation of intrinsic meaning, acceptance of horror, faith). A 2021 Frontiers study using a brief LAS found tragic optimism buffered COVID-19-era suffering, predicting lower distress and higher wellbeing beyond ordinary optimism. It is a distinct 'hope even when hope seems unwarranted' stance, not dispositional cheerfulness.",
