    description: "Grit — passion and perseverance for long-term goals — is marketed as a keystone protective trait, but Credé et al.'s 2017 meta-analysis (JPSP; 88 samples, 66,807 people) found grit correlates ρ = .84 with conscientiousness, so strongly that the two are near-redundant. Grit's link to performance is modest and driven almost entirely by the perseverance-of-effort facet, not passion/consistency-of-interest. A 2020 study bluntly labeled it 'another jangle fallacy.'",
