    feeds: ["Bodily", "Interoceptive", "Meta-Cognitive"],
    description: "Multifocal/bifocal lenses blur the ground and distort edge/depth cues underfoot, raising trip risk outdoors. The VISIBLE RCT gave active older multifocal wearers supplementary single-lens distance glasses for walking/outdoor use. In the active outdoor subgroup falls fell; overall the trial showed only an ~8% (non-significant) reduction — and the intervention appeared HARMFUL in habitually inactive wearers. A precise, counterintuitive fix for a specific person.",
