    impact: { magnitude: 2, latency: "months", durability: "sustained", effort: "low" },
    feeds: ["Bodily", "Interoceptive"],
    description: "The honest split: combined vitamin D + calcium reduces hip fracture in the frail, deficient, and institutionalized (the classic Chapuy 1992 nursing-home RCT cut hip fractures ~43%; a 2019 pooled analysis found ~16% fewer hip fractures with combined D+calcium). BUT in replete, community-dwelling elders it does essentially nothing — the 2017 JAMA meta-analysis (33 RCTs, 51,145 people) found no reduction in hip or total fractures and explicitly did 'not support routine use.' Vitamin D alone (without calcium) shows no fracture benefit.",
