    description: "Steidle & Werth (2013) found that dim illumination (~150 lux) raised insight problem-solving relative to standard office (500 lux) and bright (1,500 lux) light, an effect mediated by a heightened feeling of 'freedom from constraints' and lowered inhibition. Darkness — even merely imagined or primed — increased self-reported self-determination and risk-taking that favor idea generation.",
