    feeds: ["Creative", "Meta-Cognitive"],
    description: "A spell of dull, understimulating activity before a creative task can raise subsequent idea output — boredom appears to prompt mind-wandering and a search for stimulation that spills into divergent thinking. Mann & Cadman (2014) had participants copy numbers from a phone book (boring) before an alternative-uses task; the bored group generated more and more varied ideas than controls, with a passive/reading boring task sometimes outperforming a writing one.",
