    id: "reach-for-semantic-distance", section: "3903", title: "Push Past the First Associates (Reach for Semantic Distance)", subtitle: "practice: 'Bolsters clusters: Pattern-Recognition, Creative'",
    evidenceTag: "Moderate",
    impact: { magnitude: 2, latency: "weeks", durability: "transient", effort: "moderate" },
    feeds: ["Pattern-Recognition", "Creative"],
    description: "Original ideas live at greater semantic distance. Computational studies show the originality of a response is well predicted by how far it sits from the prompt in semantic space, and more creative people have flatter, more inter-connected associative networks that let them jump to remote concepts. The actionable move: don't stop at the obvious first associate — deliberately generate a chain of increasingly distant associations, because the creative gold is downstream of the clichés.",
