    id: "sppb-lower-extremity-function", section: "3929", title: "Lower-Extremity Physical Function (SPPB)", subtitle: "practice: 'Bolsters clusters: Independence, Falls & Hip Fracture in Older Adults, Frailty resistance'",
    evidenceTag: "Strong",
    impact: { magnitude: 3, latency: "months", durability: "sustained", effort: "moderate" },
    feeds: ["Independence / mobility", "Falls & Hip Fracture in Older Adults", "Frailty resistance", "Bodily"],
    description: "The Short Physical Performance Battery — timed standing balance, 4-metre gait speed and five chair-stands scored 0-12 — is one of the best-validated predictors of survival in older adults. In Pavasini's meta-analysis (17 studies, 16,534 people, mean age 76), scores of 0-3 carried roughly triple the mortality odds of top scores (OR ~3.25), with 4-6 (~2.1) and 7-9 (~1.5) graded in between. Because each component is trainable through strength, balance and gait work, SPPB is both a mortality gauge and a target.",
