    description: "Flavonoids — polyphenols concentrated in tea, berries, apples, dark chocolate, red wine, onions and citrus — track with lower mortality. In Bondonno's 23-year follow-up of 56,048 Danish adults, moderate habitual intake was inversely associated with all-cause, cardiovascular and cancer mortality, with the benefit plateauing near ~500 mg/day. The inverse association was notably stronger in smokers and heavy drinkers, hinting flavonoids may offset some oxidative/vascular stress.",
