    description: "The distance covered in six minutes of self-paced walking integrates cardiopulmonary, muscular and neurological function into one submaximal number, and it predicts survival. In community-living older adults, 6-minute walk distance predicted 7-year all-cause and cardiovascular mortality about as well as directly measured peak oxygen uptake (AUC ~0.74 vs ~0.73). It is a trainable capacity: aerobic and functional exercise extend it, and a shrinking distance is an early warning of decline.",
