    description: "How fast heart rate falls in the first minute after stopping exercise is a window on vagal (parasympathetic) reactivation, and it improves with aerobic training. In Cole's landmark cohort of 2,428 adults, an abnormal one-minute recovery (fall of 12 beats/min or less) roughly doubled six-year mortality risk after adjustment for workload, ejection fraction and other covariates. It is a trainable marker: aerobic conditioning speeds recovery, and a sluggish recovery flags autonomic and cardiovascular risk.",
