    description: "The assumption that whole-fat dairy is uniformly harmful is contested by large data. In the PURE cohort (136,384 adults, 21 countries), more than two daily servings of dairy versus none was associated with ~17% lower total mortality and ~22% lower major cardiovascular disease, with whole-fat dairy showing benefit rather than harm. Fermented dairy (yogurt) signals look most favorable; milk and cheese are roughly neutral.",
    callout: "Educational, not medical advice. Signal is real but MIXED and confounded: much of PURE's benefit came from lower-income countries where dairy marks affluence and better nutrition; some Western cohorts show neutral-to-adverse links for certain products. Not a green light for unlimited dairy — context and displacement matter.",
