    description: "High-dose riboflavin (400 mg/day) targets the mitochondrial energy deficit implicated in migraine. The landmark Schoenen 1998 RCT (n=55, 3 months) found 59% of riboflavin users vs 15% on placebo were 50%-responders, an NNT of 2.3 — a large effect for a cheap vitamin. Benefit takes ~2-3 months to appear and later trials/reviews are more mixed, so the AAN/AHS guideline rates it Level B ('probably effective').",
