    description: "The denomination effect: people are less likely to break a single large bill (one $100) than to spend the same value in small bills (five $20s), because large denominations feel psychologically less fungible. Across three field studies, likelihood of spending was lower with a single large denomination, and people who wanted spending self-control deliberately chose to hold large bills. It leverages the pain of paying as a deliberate brake.",
