    description: "People intuitively linearize exponential curves, so they underestimate how fast both savings AND debt compound. In Stango & Zinman's household-finance data, more-biased households borrow more, save less, and favor shorter maturities, even after controlling for income and other traits — and the bias is distinct from general financial sophistication. It quietly inflates the true cost of carried debt and shrinks the felt value of early saving.",
