    description: "Commuters randomly assigned to strike up a conversation with a stranger on a train or bus reported a more positive commute than those told to sit in solitude or behave as usual — yet a separate forecasting sample predicted exactly the opposite, expecting connection to be unpleasant. The pleasant experience held for both initiators and recipients, and people consistently underestimated strangers' willingness to talk.",
