    feeds: ["Bodily", "Interoceptive"],
    description: "The popular belief that static stretching before exercise prevents injury is not supported: meta-analyses find no reduction in all-cause or overuse injury risk from pre-activity static stretching (strengthening and proprioceptive/neuromuscular warm-ups do reduce injury). Worse, long static holds (>60 seconds per muscle) before power activities cause a small acute drop in strength, sprint, and jump performance. Static stretching does reliably increase range of motion.",
