    feeds: ["Parental", "Bodily", "Interoceptive"],
    description: "Baby-led weaning lets infants self-feed graspable whole foods instead of spoon-fed purees. The BLISS RCT (a version modified to reduce choking/iron/growth risk) found no difference vs traditional feeding in growth, BMI/overweight at 12-24 months, or iron/ferritin status, and no increase in choking with the safety-modified version. So enthusiastic claims that BLW prevents obesity or improves nutrition are not supported — it appears roughly equivalent, with possible gains in self-regulation and family-food participation.",
