    feeds: ["Prenatal health", "Bodily", "Strategic", "Systemic"],
    description: "The MRC Vitamin Study (1991), a double-blind RCT across 33 centers, showed periconceptional folic acid cut recurrence of neural-tube defects (spina bifida, anencephaly) by 72% (RR 0.28, 95% CI 0.12–0.71) in high-risk women. A subsequent Hungarian RCT (Czeizel 1992) confirmed prevention of first occurrences. This is one of the highest-payoff, lowest-cost preventive interventions known and drove worldwide food fortification.",
    callout: "Educational, not medical advice. The protective window is before and very early in pregnancy — supplementation must start before conception to work, which is the main real-world implementation gap.",
