    description: "In high-risk smokers/ex-smokers, annual low-dose CT screening cuts lung-cancer mortality. NLST (n=53,454, ≥30 pack-years) found a 20% relative reduction vs chest X-ray; NELSON (n>15,000, vs no screening) found a ~24% reduction in men (and ~33% in the smaller female group) at 10 years using volume-based nodule management. Absolute mortality benefit is meaningful because baseline risk is high in this group.",
