    description: "The strongest causal evidence is a randomized trial at Chinese travel firm Ctrip: call-center staff assigned to work from home for 9 months showed a 13% performance gain (9% from more minutes worked — fewer breaks and sick days — and 4% from more calls per minute in a quieter environment), plus higher satisfaction and halved attrition. Later evidence is more nuanced: a 2024 hybrid RCT found no productivity loss and ~35% lower quit rates, while some field studies of fully-remote knowledge work show communication and mentoring costs.",
