    feeds: ["Adversarial", "Strategic", "Social-Perceptual", "Interpersonal"],
    description: "Instead of watching body language, withhold what you already know and ask questions that let a liar contradict it — then look for statement–evidence inconsistencies. In Hartwig et al.'s training study, SUE-trained interviewers reached 85.4% deception-detection accuracy versus 56.1% for untrained interviewers, one of the largest, most replicable gains in the deception literature. It works because truth-tellers are forthcoming while liars stay avoidant.",
