    description: "Gompers, Kovner, Lerner & Scharfstein tracked VC-backed founders and found genuine performance persistence: entrepreneurs whose prior venture succeeded had roughly a 30% success rate on their next, versus about 21% for first-timers and 22% for those who previously failed. Part of the edge is skill in picking the right industry and timing to enter — 'market-timing' ability that carries across ventures — not just reputation or capital access.",
