    description: "Fairlie & Fossen distinguish opportunity entrepreneurs (who leave employment to pursue an opening) from necessity entrepreneurs (pushed in by unemployment). Using large U.S. and German datasets, 80-90% of founders are opportunity-type, and opportunity entrepreneurship is associated with more growth-oriented businesses and is pro-cyclical, while necessity entrepreneurship is counter-cyclical (rising in recessions). The motive at entry predicts the trajectory: pull beats push for growth outcomes.",
