    description: "A single-premium immediate annuity (SPIA) converts a lump sum into guaranteed lifetime income and is the cleanest hedge against outliving your money. Its distinctive engine is 'mortality credits': by pooling longevity risk, survivors are subsidized by those who die earlier, producing a payout no bond ladder can match without the pool. Yaari's classic result showed that, absent bequest motives, a rational retiree would annuitize fully; Milevsky's work quantifies when the mortality-credit advantage justifies buying.",
