    description: "Distinct from asset ALLOCATION (how much in stocks vs bonds), asset LOCATION is the tax-management choice of which holdings sit in taxable vs tax-deferred vs Roth accounts. Dammon, Spatt & Zhang (2004) modeled this formally, finding meaningful after-tax gains from placing tax-inefficient assets (e.g. taxable bonds, high-turnover funds) in tax-sheltered accounts and tax-efficient assets in taxable accounts. It raises after-tax return with no change in pre-tax risk — a modest but genuine free improvement.",
