    feeds: ["Leadership", "Interpersonal", "Meta-Cognitive", "Strategic"],
    description: "A one-word reframe changes what you get back. Across experiments (including a field study in an executive-education classroom), people prompted to give 'advice' produced more specific, critical, and actionable input than those asked for 'feedback' — because 'feedback' orients givers to evaluate past performance, while 'advice' orients them to future improvement. Cheap to apply and useful for anyone who finds solicited feedback vague and non-committal.",
