    feeds: ["Interpersonal", "Strategic", "Rhetorical", "Entrepreneurial"],
    description: "In Morris, Nadler, Kurtzberg & Thompson's 'Schmooze or lose,' pairs of unacquainted MBA students who spent ~5 minutes on the phone chatting socially — no business — before negotiating a deal entirely by email felt more rapport, formed more trusting (but no less ambitious) plans, cooperated more, competed less, and reached better economic and relational outcomes than pairs who went straight to email. A brief, cheap dose of small talk lubricates lean text channels.",
