    degrades: ["Interpersonal", "Emotional", "Community", "Intrapersonal"],
    description: "Attending to your phone while with someone ('phubbing') is a small, repeated withdrawal-of-attention that erodes connection. In Roberts & David's dyadic study, perceived partner phubbing predicted lower relationship satisfaction — mediated by conflict over phone use — and indirectly predicted lower life satisfaction and more depressive symptoms; anxiously-attached partners reported the most phone-related conflict. It functions as a micro-instance of unresponsiveness: the message received is 'this device outranks you.'",
