    impact: { magnitude: 3, latency: "days", durability: "transient", effort: "low" },
    feeds: ["Volitional", "Leadership", "Creative", "Entrepreneurial"],
    description: "Amabile & Kramer analyzed ~12,000 daily diary entries from 238 knowledge workers and found that the single most powerful boost to motivation, emotion, and creative engagement on any given day was making progress in meaningful work — even small steps. Setbacks had a correspondingly outsized negative effect. Managers who remove obstacles and mark incremental progress protect 'inner work life' and downstream performance.",
