    degrades: ["Bodily", "Volitional", "Interoceptive"],
    description: "The old advice to rest in bed for a bad back is not just useless — it slows recovery. The Cochrane review (Dahm 2010) found moderate-quality evidence that advice to stay active produces small improvements in pain and functional status versus advice to rest in bed for acute low back pain (for sciatica, little or no difference). Prolonged rest promotes deconditioning and fear-avoidance; keeping gently active is the evidence-based default. Educational, not medical advice.",
