    feeds: ["Meta-Cognitive", "Adversarial", "Logical"],
    description: "The old textbook line — 'eyewitness confidence is worthless' — is an overcorrection. Wixted & Wells (2017) synthesized the literature and showed that under 'pristine' conditions (a fair lineup, one suspect, a double-blind administrator, and confidence recorded at the first, uncontaminated identification), a high-confidence ID implies a high-accuracy ID. The honest nuance: confidence is informative only at the moment of initial retrieval and only before contaminating feedback inflates it.",
