    description: "Need for cognition (NFC) is the stable tendency to seek out and enjoy effortful thinking. Cacioppo, Petty, Feinstein & Jarvis (1996) reviewed 100+ studies: high-NFC people elaborate more on information, resist persuasion by peripheral cues, form attitudes more from argument quality, and show better recall of thought-about material. It is associated with more open, curious information processing and mastery-oriented engagement.",
