    description: "Intellectual humility — recognizing your beliefs might be wrong and valuing others' intellectual strengths — is a stable, measurable disposition tied to openness, curiosity, tolerance of ambiguity, low dogmatism, and better attunement to argument strength (Leary et al. 2017). The intellectually humble are more open to learning opposing views and expose themselves to more counter-attitudinal information (Porter & Schumann 2018), and a growth mindset of intelligence can boost humility, which in turn boosts openness.",
