    description: "Grossmann's 'wise reasoning' bundles intellectual humility, recognition that situations change, awareness of uncertainty, and integration of multiple perspectives. It predicts greater life satisfaction, less negative affect, better relationships, and lower depressive rumination — and, notably, it did so better than raw IQ (Grossmann et al. 2013). It is also state-sensitive and context-dependent: people reason more wisely about others' dilemmas than their own, and self-distancing raises wise reasoning (Brienza et al. 2018, situated measurement).",
