    description: "Warm-up decrement is the transient drop in skilled performance at the start of a session or after an extended rest within one — a substitution, a rain delay, an intermission. Nacson and Schmidt's (1971) activity-set hypothesis explains it as the temporary loss of an 'activity set': arousal, attentional attunement, and movement timing that must be re-established. It is not skill loss; it is a state that needs reinstating.",
