    description: "Bonanno's trajectory research overturned the assumption that trauma usually breaks people. Across bereavement, disaster, injury and violence, the single most common response is a resilient trajectory — stable healthy functioning — reported in roughly 35–65% of exposed samples, larger than the chronic-distress group. Most people exposed to a potentially traumatic event do NOT develop PTSD; the population base rate of PTSD after trauma is well under half. Knowing this is itself protective: pathologizing normal distress ('everyone is traumatized') can undermine the natural recovery most people would otherwise show.",
