    impact: { magnitude: 2, latency: "months", durability: "sustained", effort: "low" },
    feeds: ["Emotional", "Intrapersonal", "Meta-Cognitive"],
    description: "Older adults preferentially attend to and remember positive over negative information relative to younger adults. A meta-analysis of 100 studies (N=7,129) found a reliable age-related shift, but it is modest (roughly g≈0.2–0.3) and appears mainly when cognitive resources are unconstrained — it depends on intact executive control and is deployed toward emotionally meaningful goals as future time feels limited.",
