    description: "Baltes's SOC model describes adaptive life management under age-related losses: narrowing goals (selection), investing effort in what matters (optimization), and using aids/substitute means for what's lost (compensation). People reporting more SOC use score higher on subjective wellbeing, positive affect, life satisfaction, and lower loneliness, and show better functional outcomes (fewer falls/sick days) — the positive mirror of maladaptive, resource-squandering aging.",
