    feeds: ["Meta-Cognitive", "Volitional", "Community"],
    description: "Retirement's cognitive effect is genuinely mixed. Consistent with 'use it or lose it,' people who leave complex, mentally demanding jobs decline more slowly, and 'bridge employment' (gradual part-time/second-career exit, especially switching employers and learning new skills) is associated with less post-retirement cognitive decline than abrupt full retirement. Yet other analyses find retirement can improve wellbeing and reduce stress — outcome depends on what replaces the job's stimulation.",
