    description: "A cornerstone honesty check on motivation-first models (Theory of Planned Behavior, education campaigns): experimentally boosting people's intentions only weakly moves their behavior. Webb & Sheeran's (2006) meta-analysis of 47 experiments found a medium-to-large change in intention (d = 0.66) produced only a small-to-medium change in behavior (d = 0.36); roughly half of people who form an intention fail to act on it. Interventions that change only attitudes and intentions — without capability, opportunity, or planning support — routinely underdeliver.",
