    description: "A systematic review of intervention studies (Gerbild 2018) found that ~160 minutes/week of moderate-to-vigorous aerobic exercise for 6 months meaningfully improves erectile function in men whose ED is driven by inactivity, obesity, hypertension, metabolic syndrome, or cardiovascular disease. The mechanism is endothelial and vascular: erections are a hemodynamic event, so the same training that improves arterial health improves arterial erections. Effect is real but moderate and concentrated in vasculogenic/lifestyle-related ED.",
