    description: "Shubik's dollar auction auctions a $1 bill to the highest bidder, but the second-highest bidder ALSO pays their last bid and gets nothing. Rational-looking incremental bids trap both players into paying far more than a dollar — Shubik's classroom record was over $200 for $1. It is the pure structure of escalation: an all-pay auction / war of attrition where, once committed, each side's best local move keeps them bidding. The strategic lesson is defensive — recognize all-pay dynamics early and refuse to enter, because the only reliable winning move is often not to play.",
